.4.4 provisioned through mise.\\n22: \\n23: - Worktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a`, branch `jolt-j0a` from master `212c45dd9`. Changes are uncommitted and nothing is staged.\\n24: - Logs: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/build/j0a-logs/` (untracked `build/`).\\n25: \\n26: ## Environment\\n27: - Darwin arm64, macOS 26.6.2, Apple clang 21.0.0, babashka v1.13.223.\\n28: - Chez 10.4.1 (threaded `#t`) at `~/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme`.\\n29: - CMake 4.4.4: `mise install cmake` was run this round. It went into the shared mise install dir at `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`. This is the only thing installed outside the worktree.\\n30: \\n31: ## 1. Pinned jolt and Chez from a tracked declaration: DONE\\n32: \\n33: - **`jolt-toolchain.edn`** (new, tracked, repo root) records:\\n34:   - the jolt origin `https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt`, full SHA `96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63`, and commit date;\\n35:   - `:tag :none`, nearest release tag `v0.8.23` (`a0ac71c3f638fe55158bd01b4ecbb0dd3d7545e5`), describe string `vnightly-16-g96d7b866` (ruling 4);\\n36:   - all 7 recursive submodule SHAs (`git submodule status --recursive` on the pinned tree);\\n37:   - `:patches []` (default 2: none);\\n38:   - Chez `10.4.1` via mise, required threaded;\\n39:   - CMake `4.4.4` via mise;\\n40:   - the observed macOS paths and compiler.\\n41:   - Linux is `nil` (not run). `:native {}` (libblake3, ANTLR4 C++ and libcrypto are later rounds).\\n42: - **`mise.toml`** (worktree copy): `chezscheme = \\\"10.4.1\\\"` and `cmake = \\\"4.4.4\\\"`, exact pins. CMake 4.4.4 is what `mise latest cmake` resolved. The main tree's uncommitted `chezscheme = \\\"latest\\\"` was not touched.\\n43:   - The brief states the owner confirmed the exact-Chez default. §13.2 W6 also asks for that acceptance to be **recorded in §13.2 of the design doc**. I did not edit docs, so the orchestrator should record it there.\\n44: - **`bb bootstrap:jolt`** (new `bb.edn` task, running `src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj`):\\n45:   - **Toolchain check:** checks Chez and CMake through `mise exec <tool>@<pinned> -- which`. It verifies the exact versions and that Chez is threaded, and never installs anything.\\n46:   - **Clone:** if `build/tools/jolt` is absent, it clones the origin, checks out the full SHA detached, and initializes submodules recursively.\\n47:   - **Verify:** the HEAD SHA, a clean tree, and all submodule SHAs against the declaration.\\n48:   - **Env file:** writes `build/tools/jolt-env.sh` with `JOLT_CHEZ` set explicitly (plus `JOLT_HOME`).\\n49:   - **Smoke:** runs `jolt -e '(+ 1 2)'` and expects 3.\\n50:   - **Never pulls:** an existing checkout is only verified.\\n51:   - Nothing downloads during namespace loading.\\n52: - **Evidence:**\\n53: \\n54: | Run | Result | Log |\\n55: |---|---|---|\\n56: | Cold (`rm -rf build/tools/jolt`, then `bb bootstrap:jolt`) | exit 0, real **153.71 s** | `bootstrap-cold.log` |\\n57: | Warm (existing checkout verified, no network) | exit 0, real **7.12 s** | `bootstrap-warm.log` |\\n58: | Negative: HEAD moved to `a0ac71c3` | exit 1, `…is at a0ac71c3…, declared 96d7b866…; ordinary runs never pull` | `bootstrap-neg-head.log` |\\n59: | Negative: one edit to the checkout's README | exit 1, `has local changes: M README.md` | `bootstrap-neg-dirty.log` |\\n60: | Restored | exit 0 | `bootstrap-restored.log` |\\n61: \\n62: ## 2. `:jolt` alias and `src/jolt` root: PARTIAL\\n63: \\n64: **2a. Done.**\\n65: - `deps.edn` gains `:jolt {:replace-paths [\\\"src/jolt\\\" \\\"src/cljc\\\" \\\"src/clj\\\"] :replace-deps {}}`. It has no `build/antlr` Java classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no dependency coordinates.\\n66: - `jolt -Srepro -Spath -A:jolt` gives exactly `…/src/jolt:…/src/cljc:…/src/clj`, in that order (`spath.log`).\\n67: - `-Stree -A:jolt` prints nothing, so the resolved dependency set is empty. That was verified, not assumed.\\n68: - New tracked root `src/jolt/` holds only a README stating the §4.1 rules. No host override is needed for this closure.\\n69: - The alias only lists `src/clj`. The `:jolt` guards on `yin.repl.host` and `dao.space.dht` (§4.2) are not done; they matter once the closure reaches them.\\n70: \\n71: **2b. NOT DONE: the spike overlay fold.**\\n72: - The four overlay files (`build/jolt-spike/overlay/`) all modify forbidden namespaces:\\n73:   - `dao/jing.cljc`\\n74:   - `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`\\n75:   - `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`\\n76:   - `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`\\n77: - The brief says \\\"do NOT edit shared dao.stream / dao.data / dao.jing / yin.vm source (the exception: none this round)\\\", and folding them needs exactly those edits, or `.jolt` copies of `dao.jing.cbor`, which §4.1 forbids. I followed the explicit prohibition and folded nothing.\\n78: - Two of the overlays must not be folded as they are anyway:\\n79:   - The `dao.jing` overlay stubs SHA-256 with a throw, and the brief allows no stubs.\\n80:   - The `integer/host` overlay's bigint `bit-and`/`bit-or`/`bit-xor` are knowingly wrong (§4.4, §5.1).\\n81: - None of the four is needed for the baseline closure (item 3).\\n82: - **The orchestrator must decide which slice may edit `dao.jing`/`yin.vm` for the fold (J0a round 2 or J1).** Attribution for that fold: the spike session (claude-opus-5-5, 2026-10-19), `collab/1792412960461-engineer-jolt-yin-repl-spike.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md` section 5.\\n83: \\n84: ## 3. `yang.antlr.export` and `yang.antlr.packet` load without overlays: DONE\\n85: \\n86: - `bb smoke:jolt` runs `build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj` with the env file sourced. Every run exited 0 with `SUMMARY ok` (`smoke-1.log`, `smoke-2.log`).\\n87: - **Closure:** loading `yang.antlr.export` adds exactly `(yang.antlr.export yang.antlr.packet)` to `loaded-libs`. That is asserted.\\n88: - **Transit:** none. Nothing from `dao.data`, `dao.stream.transit` or `cognitect.transit` is reached. A separate check found no loaded lib matching `transit|cognitect`. So there is nothing to record as a runtime-loaded transit dependency for this closure.\\n89: - **Values:**\\n90:   - `packet/code-points \\\"aé😀\\\"` = `[97 233 128512]`. This runs the `:clj` branch, `.codePoints` via jolt's String shim, and passes unchanged.\\n91:   - `packet/utf8-bytes` gives 7.\\n92:   - `export/byte-offsets [97 233 128512]` gives `[0 1 3 7]`.\\n93: \\n94: ## 4. defcfn `:blocking` smoke: DONE (collect-safety not established)\\n95: \\n96: - **Assertions** in `src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj`:\\n97:   - `usleep` bound `:blocking` returns 0 after at least 200 ms (observed 201 and 204 ms).\\n98:   - `strlen` bound `:blocking` on the UTF-8 C string \\\"aé😀\\\" returns 7.\\n99:   - Both PASS.\\n100: - **Collect timing, RECORD only (not asserted).** A full collection (`jolt.host/gc-full!`) ran on the main thread while another thread was inside `usleep(400 ms)`:\\n101: \\n102: | Call binding | collect start | collect end | call end |\\n103: |---|---|---|---|\\n104: | `:blocking` | 50 ms | 118 ms | 400 ms |\\n105: | plain (no `:blocking`) | 57 ms | 212 ms | 410 ms |\\n106: \\n107: - **Anomaly:** jolt's own documentation (`stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj:1502-1510`) says a thread in a non-`:blocking` call stays active and the collector waits until the call returns. The plain control did not wait for the call to return. I reproduced this with a raw `Thread` as well as `future`.\\n108: - So this observation cannot yet show that `:blocking` is what makes a call collect-safe. I removed my first version of the check, which asserted it, after the control falsified it.\\n109: - Possible explanations, none verified: the rendezvous path in `sa-gc-collect` (`host/chez/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:61-80`), or Chez handling of a thread in `usleep`.\\n110: - The long-hash collect-safety gate (§6.3) is later J0a work and will need a mechanism that discriminates.\\n111: \\n112: ## Commands run (foreground, in the worktree)\\n113: ```\\n114: git worktree add /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a -b jolt-j0a master   # from the repo root\\n115: mise trust\\n116: mise latest cmake            # 4.4.4\\n117: mise install cmake\\n118: bb bootstrap:jolt            # cold, warm, two negatives, restored (logs above)\\n119: bb smoke:jolt                # x2 (first with a fresh JOLT_CACHE_DIR; source mode keeps JOLT_AOT_CACHE=0, so no cache was written)\\n120: . build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME\\\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -Spath -A:jolt\\n121: \\\"$JOLT_HOME\\\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -Stree -A:jolt\\n122: mise exec -- cljstyle check/fix src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj jolt-toolchain.edn deps.edn\\n123: ```\\n124: - **Wall clock:** bootstrap cold 153.71 s, warm 7.12 s; smoke 7.77 s and then 7.45 s. jolt runs from source, so there is no AOT cache and cold and warm are similar.\\n125: - **cljstyle:** my new files pass. `deps.edn` and `bb.edn` already fail `cljstyle check` on master (I checked `git show master:deps.edn`), and none of the reported lines are mine.\\n126: - **npm ci:** not needed.\\n127: \\n128: ## J0a acceptance items NOT done this round (not started)\\n129: - Recording the owner's acceptance of the exact-Chez default in §13.2. The value is applied in `mise.toml` and the toolchain file, but this is a doc edit for the orchestrator.\\n130: - Folding the spike overlays (2b, blocked by the brief) and the rest of the §4.4 fold/audit sites, including the machine-readable branch inventory and the reached-`src/clj` guard list (`yin.repl.host`, `dao.space.dht`).\\n131: - Clean-cache core require of `yin.repl` without overlays. The standard/main dependency audit naming runtime-unexercised dependencies (`cognitect.transit` via `dao.data` and others).\\n132: - Reproducing the S arithmetic and the six hashes.\\n133: - Vendored native sources: libblake3 and ANTLR4 C++ revisions and hashes, `bb build:jolt-native`, output