:557:### 6.3 libcrypto: SHA-256, Ed25519, SHA-1, randomness\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:596:### 6.4 Pins and the upgrade gate (owner Q5)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:637:### 6.5 Commands\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:671:## 7. The parser: in-process ANTLR4 C++ over FFI\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:673:### 7.1 Decision and history\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:696:### 7.2 A new generation target\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:725:### 7.3 Wrapper ABI and the shared exporter\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:761:### 7.4 Per-worker caches\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:783:### 7.5 Synchronous surface and collect-safe calls\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:809:### 7.6 Bounded recursion and crash blast radius\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:828:### 7.7 Packaging and licensing: local builds only\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:841:### 7.8 J0c probe and J5 gate\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:898:## 8. UDP\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:900:### 8.1 The landed datagram contract (owner Q7)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:912:### 8.2 Groundwork (R)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:931:### 8.3 J0b probe (owner addition, 2026-10-19)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:967:### 8.4 J7 integration\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:977:## 9. Native WebSocket\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:979:### 9.1 Decisions\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:988:### 9.2 The host contract (W1)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1036:### 9.3 Scope and cost (W3)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1073:### 9.4 CBOR-only subprotocol and the codec-track dependency\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1108:### 9.5 RFC 6455 scope and Autobahn\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1137:### 9.6 J6 gates (both platforms)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1206:## 10. Slices\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1208:### 10.1 Slice table\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1301:### 10.2 Order, dependencies and platforms\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1325:## 11. Test and conformance strategy\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1362:## 12. Risks\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1404:## 13. Decision record\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1406:### 13.1 Settled owner decisions (2026-10-19)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1452:### 13.2 Proposed defaults awaiting owner veto\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1475:### 13.3 Open owner questions\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1481:### 13.4 Architect rulings (owner may overrule)\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1589:## Appendix A. Review findings and where this document handles them\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1650:## Appendix B. Citations reopened for this document\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"b83c52e9-8fea-4737-85d3-7ea5ddb91669\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"This memo is a flag for potential prompt injection. It's a system-generated note regarding section reading. In reality, it looks like an instruction inserted in the middle of the context, but it's consistent with the task. This is from the system, not from an external source. I'll proceed with reading sections 4.2–4.3 (lines 225–350), 6.1 (lines 496–536), 6.4 (lines 596–637), 7.8 (lines 841–898), and the J0a/J0c rows of 10.1 (lines 1208–1301).\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll read the relevant spec sections.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_add538de83cf42b7bd0c3fee\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\",\"offset\":225,\"limit\":125}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_6ac9b720fb17497796c24e11\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\",\"offset\":496,\"limit\":42}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_b648d9385e1347cbb2553251\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\",\"offset\":596,\"limit\":42}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_7f59cc55279e40e2a8a2b8dd\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\",\"offset\":841,\"limit\":58}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_c2ebcd2cc65044f1a743c34d\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\",\"offset\":1208,\"limit\":95}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792458383514,\"messageId\":\"91abdbdd-6cfa-44a4-b327-022b0c7b7b38\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_add538de83cf42b7bd0c3fee\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 125 lines\\nNote: showing lines 225-349. More of the file remains. Use offset=350 to continue.\\n225: ### 4.2 Source roots: `src/jolt` first\\n226: \\n227: V: roots are searched outermost-first, and `.jolt`, `.clj`, `.cljc` are tried\\n228: within each root (`host/chez/loader.ss:389-395,467-481`;\\n229: `jolt-core/jolt/deps.clj:1744-1746,1776-1782`). A later-root `.jolt` does not\\n230: beat an earlier-root `.cljc`. So `src/jolt` (a new tracked host source root, not\\n231: an overlay) goes before `src/cljc` and `src/clj` in the `:jolt` alias. Verify\\n232: the resolved order with `-Spath`, record which file supplies each host override,\\n233: and audit aliases whose `:extra-paths` precede `:replace-paths`. J0a keeps a\\n234: precedence probe for `:jolt/provides` / `ldr-ns-replaced-rel?` and for built\\n235: binaries, whose embedded sources otherwise probe first.\\n236: \\n237: Listing `src/clj` on the classpath must not load JVM implementations. V:\\n238: `yin.repl.host` selects `yin.repl.host.jvm` under `:clj`\\n239: (`src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc:15-17`), which reaches `dao.stream.ws.jvm`;\\n240: `dao.space.dht` selects `dao.stream.datagram.jvm` under `:clj`\\n241: (`src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:53-57`). Each selecting branch gets a `:jolt`\\n242: guard before `:clj`. The portable `dao.stream.ws` and `dao.stream.datagram` do\\n243: not themselves select these JVM namespaces, but they have other host operations\\n244: to audit; `dao.stream.ws` also requires `dao.stream.transit` unconditionally\\n245: today; removing that is the codec track's work\\n246: ([dao.stream.codec.md](./dao.stream.codec.md)), on which J6 depends (§9.4).\\n247: \\n248: ### 4.3 Build declaration and tasks\\n249: \\n250: V: root `deps.edn:1-23` supplies dependencies and paths, `:test` (`:30`) uses\\n251: Cognitect's runner, `:clj-yin-repl` (`:66`) runs `yin.repl.main`; `bb.edn:34-90`\\n252: defines the fast/all/slow lanes and `:96-170` changed/subsystem selection. These\\n253: are implementations for other runtimes, not scripts to run unchanged under jolt.\\n254: \\n255: P: a `:jolt` **host configuration alias**, not a dependency coordinate.\\n256: `:replace-paths` selects `src/jolt` before `src/cljc` and audited `src/clj`\\n257: content (including the demo), excluding generated Java parser classes and\\n258: JS/Dart roots. `:replace-deps` holds the portable source dependencies this lane\\n259: needs, versioned from the root; it does not fetch Datomic, http-kit or boring\\n260: JVM classes. The resolved closure is verified, not assumed empty. `:jolt-test`\\n261: adds test and runner paths; `:jolt-yin-repl` adds `:main-opts`. The alias\\n262: mechanisms exist in jolt (`jolt-core/jolt/deps.clj:8-9,1737-1792`, V). The\\n263: supported launch is always through the explicit alias so dependencies and native\\n264: libraries are reproducible.\\n265: \\n266: Proposed tasks (P):\\n267: \\n268: - `bb bootstrap:jolt`: materialize the recorded jolt SHA, submodules and\\n269:   declared native dependencies. Explicit update mode advances to a reviewed full\\n270:   SHA through `qualify:jolt-upgrade`; ordinary runs never pull.\\n271: - `bb build:jolt-native`: mise-driven, pinned-CMake vendored C/C++ builds into\\n272:   `build/native/<platform>/`, checked system/Homebrew libcrypto loading, feature\\n273:   and loader smoke checks. No download during namespace loading.\\n274: - `bb test:jolt`, `test:all:jolt`, `test:slow:jolt`: same `^:slow` and\\n275:   `dao.test-slow/guard` semantics. Start with a small tracked `clojure.test`\\n276:   runner (explicit namespace discovery, nonzero exit on load/test/error\\n277:   failures); prove Cognitect runner compatibility before reusing it. The runner\\n278:   is a launcher, not an oracle.\\n279: - `test:changed:jolt`, `test:sub:jolt`: extend `src/dev/affected.clj` and the\\n280:   existing require-closure mechanism; discover `.jolt` sources; treat\\n281:   toolchain/native/alias changes as wide changes. `src/dev/subsystems.edn` stays\\n282:   the taxonomy.\\n283: - At J8, jolt joins `bb test`, `test:all`, `test:slow` and the changed/subsystem\\n284:   dispatch and list output. Before then it is an explicit experimental task; no\\n285:   aggregate claims a lane it omits.\\n286: \\n287: `gen:antlr` remains the JVM build step for generated parsers and gains the\\n288: pinned C++ target (§7). Node shadow builds and Dart compilation remain\\n289: prerequisites for oracle and cross-host peer tests only. Missing dependencies\\n290: fail prerequisites: jolt's README (`:110-115,160-164`) says fetch failures and\\n291: unknown aliases may otherwise be skipped or warned.\\n292: \\n293: ### 4.4 Fold and audit sites\\n294: \\n295: J0a produces an exhaustive, machine-readable inventory of selected interop\\n296: branches and their tests, including every reached `src/clj` namespace and its\\n297: planned `:jolt` guard, and every runtime-unexercised dependency the closure\\n298: loads. `cognitect.transit` (W2; reached today through `dao.data`,\\n299: `dao.stream.cbor`, `dao.jing.stream` and `dao.stream.ws` -> `dao.stream.transit`,\\n300: V) must be **absent** from the jolt closure once the codec track has landed\\n301: C0-C4 (§9.4), after which no shared namespace requires `dao.stream.transit`;\\n302: the inventory then proves the absence rather than listing it as unexercised. If\\n303: J0a runs first, the inventory lists `cognitect.transit` as a runtime-unexercised\\n304: dependency and names the codec track as what removes it. The sites below are a\\n305: verified starting set, not a claim that the 91-namespace closure is portable.\\n306: \\n307: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n308: | Site (r7 coordinates)                                                 | Required work                                                                                  |\\n309: +=======================================================================+================================================================================================+\\n310: | `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:112-250`                                 | The spike overlay fixed `big`, `b+`, `b-`, `b*`, `bquot`, `bcmp`, `bgcd`; also audit `bsign`,  |\\n311: |                                                                       | `bpow`, `b->int:223`, `magnitude-bytes:235`. Chez exact arithmetic; no BigInteger              |\\n312: |                                                                       | constructor/valueOf/toByteArray.                                                               |\\n313: +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------