ownload/compiler selection; inventory its scripts before enabling it. Devboot\\n532: and `jolt build` record compiler/provisioning checksums, use the same Chez and\\n533: discard caches on runtime/source change. Source-mode execution is the baseline;\\n534: AOT packaging is an additional gate, never the fix for a semantic failure.\\n535: \\n536: ### 6.2 BLAKE3 over FFI\\n537: \"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_b648d9385e1347cbb2553251\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 42 lines\\nNote: showing lines 596-637. More of the file remains. Use offset=638 to continue.\\n596: ### 6.4 Pins and the upgrade gate (owner Q5)\\n597: \\n598: Owner: \\\"record the mob's answer\\\", then \\\"opus when needed\\\". Jolt is pinned by\\n599: full SHA in `jolt-toolchain.edn`; a suitable release-tagged SHA is preferred;\\n600: main remains the upstream development source; nothing updates silently. The\\n601: owner or orchestrator triggers the proposed `bb qualify:jolt-upgrade` when an\\n602: upstream fix we need lands, when the resolved Chez version changes, or when the\\n603: pin is older than about 30 days. Age triggers evaluation, not promotion; a\\n604: failing candidate leaves the last passing pin.\\n605: \\n606: The gate runs on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64: clean tracked load and resolved\\n607: paths; relevant fast/all/slow tests with counts; J1 integer/CBOR/hash fixtures;\\n608: shared VM boundary traces; J0b UDP and J0c parser/GC/cache/lifetime regressions;\\n609: native-library provenance; J6/J7 peers once they exist. It records candidate,\\n610: base and submodule SHAs, exact Chez, patches, native versions, commands, results\\n611: and rollback coordinates. No unavailable test passes silently. Early pins\\n612: qualify only for the implemented milestone; J8 promotion needs every parity\\n613: gate. No numeric JVM-ratio budget exists before J8 evidence.\\n614: \\n615: Pin and tag (W7; ruled, §13.4 ruling 4). V (read-only git in the l