 my own role/model.\\n\\nFindings:\\n\\nF1 LOW — jolt-toolchain.edn:44 :observed :cmake-path records `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/bin/cmake`, but the bootstrap log shows the actual path as `.../cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake` (bootstrap-neg-*.log:2; report line 29 agrees with the log, and the toolchain file disagrees). The tracked observation record is wrong. Fix: record the actual path (or remove the :cmake-path detail).\\n\\nF2 LOW — src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj verify!: never checks the clone's origin remote against the declared :origin at all. An existing checkout with the correct SHA/submodule but planted from a different origin will pass. Fix: `(= origin (sh \\\"git\\\" \\\"-C\\\" dir \\\"remote\\\" \\\"get-url\\\" \\\"origin\\\"))`.\\n\\nF3 LOW (process) — worktree pins chezscheme in mise.toml to \\\"10.4.1\\\", but §6.4 (lines 630-635) says exact pinning is proposal default 3, unresolved; the J0a row in 10.1 makes recording the owner's disposition a precondition. The author has disclosed this; the orchestrator must record the disposition in §13.2 before merging, otherwise the pin violates \\\"nobody changes selectors\\\".\\n\\nF4 INFO — No log of the `-Stree -A:jolt` empty-tree verification (only spath.log). Report claims verified; the evidence is not retained. Also the report says usleep \\\"observed values are 201 and 204 ms\\\", but the log shows 205 and 200. Harmless but the numbers aren't quoted from the retained logs.\\n\\nF5 INFO — The dirty check uses `git status --porcelain`, which misses gitignored tampering inside the clone (e.g., replaced build artifacts); acceptable as a baseline; note for hardening the gate in §6.4. Also if clone is interrupted, an unusable directory remains, and it fails on git's error rather than a re-clone — acceptable.\\n\\nPositive verifications:\\n- Pins match §6.4 ruling 4 exactly (sha, :tag :none, v0.8.23/a0ac71c3, describe).\\n- Submodule map equivalence check fails on extra/missing