oolchain.edn diff = only the cmake-path line. Other files (bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, jolt_smoke.clj, src/jolt/README.md) — I should quickly re-check that they're unchanged. jolt_smoke.clj: does F4 also relate to the report citations rather than the smoke file? The log shows the same structure. I could re-read these to confirm no changes, but read_file's \\\"unchanged\\\" note would help: re-reading the same window of unchanged files returns a short note. Let me re-read jolt_smoke.clj, bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, src/jolt/README.md, and the r2 report.\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me confirm the remaining declared files are untouched and check the r2 report's quoted numbers.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_71cf356907514e598df5494f\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"paths\":[\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/bb.edn\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/deps.edn\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/mise.toml\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/jolt/README.md\"]}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_47b6aa5c61f14c10aa6e478b\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"ms|observed|20[0-9] |21[0-9]\",\"path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-n\":true}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792458940712,\"messageId\":\"fc803d81-e25f-4bee-8b22-db7496a08d74\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_71cf356907514e598df5494f\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 5/5 files\\n--- File Contents ---\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/bb.edn (unknown)\\n{:tasks\\n {gen:antlr\\n  {:doc \\\"Generate the pinned grammars-v4 parsers for every target (antlr/*/manifest.edn): Java compiled into build/antlr/<g>/classes, JavaScript in build/antlr/<g>/js, Dart in lib/antlr/<g>; filters after --: --grammar g --target t\\\"\\n   :task (apply shell \\\"clojure\\\" \\\"-M:antlr-gen\\\" *command-line-args*)}\\n\\n  ;; jolt host lane (experimental, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md)\\n  bootstrap:jolt\\n  {:doc \\\"Materialize the jolt-toolchain.edn pins into build/tools/jolt (mise Chez/CMake checked, jolt cloned at the full SHA, never pulled) and write build/tools/jolt-env.sh\\\"\\n   :task (System/exit\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\\\")))}\\n\\n  smoke:jolt\\n  {:doc \\\"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\\\"\\n   :task (System/exit\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\"sh\\\" \\\"-c\\\"\\n                         \\\". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\\\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\\\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\\\")))}\\n\\n  build:yin-repl-node\\n  {:doc \\\"Compile the Node yin.repl (shadow-cljs build :yin-repl) to target/yin-repl.js\\\"\\n   ;; The Node lanes (test:cljs and its variants) depend on this task, so the\\n   ;; generated JavaScript parser reaches them through it.\\n   :depends [gen:antlr]\\n   ;; yin.repl.dht-process-test spawns it as the JVM-to-Node reader of\\n   ;; DHT epic S5, a required leg: a missing build fails that test.\\n   :task (shell \\\"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl\\\")}\\n\\n  build:yin-repl-peer\\n  {:doc \\\"Compile the yin.repl R5 cross-host peer (client role and --serve server role) as a Dart exe\\\"\\n   ;; The Dart lanes depend on this task, so the generated Dart parser\\n   ;; reaches them through it.\\n   :depends [gen:antlr]\\n   ;; Process B of the R5 slice is a whole program rather than a test\\n   ;; namespace, and this project's cljd.core carries the Flutter extensions,\\n   ;; so only an ahead-of-time build is a peer the plain Dart VM can start.\\n   ;; It is compiled alone and first: the test build rewrites the same\\n   ;; cljd-out tree, so a peer built after it would import a tree it does\\n   ;; not match.  The R5 cross-host tests spawn this one exe from the JVM\\n   ;; and Node lanes, so `bb test` builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or\\n   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\\n   ;; rather than failing.\\n   :task (do (shell \\\"mkdir -p build\\\")\\n             (shell \\\"clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile yin.repl.slice-peer\\\")\\n             (shell \\\"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\\\"))}\\n\\n  ;; Fast default lanes: no ^:slow test, no dao.test-slow/guard body.\\n  test:clj {:doc \\\"JVM tests, fast: skips ^:slow ones; the DHT process test needs the Node REPL build\\\"\\n            :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\\n            :task (shell \\\"clojure -M:test -e :slow\\\")}\\n\\n  test:cljs {:doc \\\"Node tests, fast: dao.test-slow guarded bodies print SKIP; needs the Node REPL build\\\"\\n             :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\\n             :task (shell \\\"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\\\")}\\n\\n  test:cljd {:doc \\\"Dart tests, fast: aggregated shards via src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; guarded bodies print SKIP\\\"\\n             :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\\n             :task (shell \\\"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\\\")}\\n\\n  ;; Every test, slow ones included (about 20+ minutes on the JVM).\\n  test:all:clj {:doc \\\"Every JVM test, ^:slow included (20+ minutes); for unattended runs\\\"\\n                :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\\n                :task (shell \\\"clojure -M:test\\\")}\\n\\n  test:all:cljs {:doc \\\"Every Node test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\\\"\\n                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\\n                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\\\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\\\" \\\"1\\\"}}\\n                              \\\"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\\\")}\\n\\n  test:all:cljd {:doc \\\"Every Dart test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\\\"\\n                 :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\\n                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\\\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\\\" \\\"1\\\"}}\\n                              \\\"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\\\")}\\n\\n  ;; Only the slow tests. Node and Dart select by namespace, so the other\\n  ;; tests inside the nine namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard also run.\\n  test:slow:clj {:doc \\\"Only the ^:slow JVM tests (about 14 minutes for long-loops-test); for unattended runs\\\"\\n                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\\n                 :task (shell \\\"clojure -M:test -i :slow\\\")}\\n\\n  test:slow:cljs {:doc \\\"Node: only namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\\\"\\n                  :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\\n                  :task (let [re (-> (shell {:out :string}\\n                                            \\\"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-regex\\\")\\n                                     :out\\n                                     clojure.string/trim)]\\n                          (shell {:extra-env {\\\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\\\" \\\"1\\\"}}\\n                                 \\\"clj\\\" \\\"-M:cljs\\\" \\\"-m\\\" \\\"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\\\"\\n                                 \\\"compile\\\" \\\"test\\\" \\\"--config-merge\\\"\\n                                 (str \\\"{:ns-regexp \\\\\\\"\\\" re \\\"\\\\\\\"}\\\")))}\\n\\n  test:slow:cljd {:doc \\\"Dart: only generated tests of namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\\\"\\n                  :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\\n                  :task (shell {:extra-env {\\\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\\\" \\\"1\\\"}}\\n                               \\\"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-only\\\")}\\n\\n  test:slow {:doc \\\"Only the slow tests on every lane: JVM by tag, Node and Dart by namespace\\\"\\n             :depends [test:slow:clj test:slow:cljs test:slow:cljd]}\\n\\n  test:all {:doc \\\"Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM, Node, Dart)\\\"\\n            :depends [test:all:clj test:all:cljs test:all:cljd]}\\n\\n  test {:doc \\\"All three lanes in their fast default form (JVM, Node, Dart)\\\"\\n        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}\\n\\n  ;; Only the tests a change can affect (src/dev/affected.clj): the\\n  ;; reverse require closure of the changed files since the merge-base\\n  ;; with master. Extra args pass through (--base REF, --changed FILE...).\\n  ;; Exit 2 on a wide change (deps.edn, bb.edn, src/dev/, ...): run bb test.\\n  test:changed {:doc \\\"Fast tests a change can affect, three lanes in parallel\\\"\\n                :task (System/exit\\n                        (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                      \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                      *command-line-args*)))}\\n\\n  test:changed:clj {:doc \\\"JVM lane of test:changed\\\"\\n                    :task (System/exit\\n                            (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                          \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                          \\\"--lane\\\" \\\"clj\\\" *command-line-args*)))}\\n\\n  test:changed:cljs {:doc \\\"Node lane of test:changed\\\"\\n                     :task (System/exit\\n                             (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                           \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                           \\\"--lane\\\" \\\"cljs\\\"\\n                                           *command-line-args*)))}\\n\\n  test:changed:cljd {:doc \\\"Dart lane of test:changed\\\"\\n                     :task (System/exit\\n                             (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                           \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                           \\\"--lane\\\" \\\"cljd\\\"\\n                                           *command-line-args*)))}\\n\\n  test:changed:list {:doc \\\"What test:changed would run and why; runs nothing\\\"\\n                     :task (System/exit\\n                             (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                           \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                           \\\"--list\\\" *command-line-args*)))}\\n\\n  ;; Subsystem tests (src/dev/affected.clj): canonical subsystems defined\\n  ;; in src/dev/subsystems.edn. Positional arguments name subsystems; flags\\n  ;; pass through (--lane L, --list, --slow).\\n  test:sub {:doc \\\"Subsystem tests, three lanes in parallel: bb test:sub <subsystem>... [--slow]\\\"\\n            :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \\\"--\\\")))\\n                                                 *command-line-args*)\\n                        sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\\\"--subsystem\\\" s]) subs)]\\n                    (System/exit\\n                      (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                    \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                    (concat sub-args flags)))))}\\n\\n  test:sub:clj {:doc \\\"JVM lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:clj <subsystem>... [--slow]\\\"\\n                :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \\\"--\\\")))\\n                                                     *command-line-args*)\\n                            sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\\\"--subsystem\\\" s]) subs)]\\n                        (System/exit\\n                          (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                        \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                        \\\"--lane\\\" \\\"clj\\\"\\n                                        (concat sub-args flags)))))}\\n\\n  test:sub:cljs {:doc \\\"Node lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>... [--slow]\\\"\\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \\\"--\\\")))\\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\\\"--subsystem\\\" s]) subs)]\\n                         (System/exit\\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                         \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                         \\\"--lane\\\" \\\"cljs\\\"\\n                                         (concat sub-args flags)))))}\\n\\n  test:sub:cljd {:doc \\\"Dart lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>... [--slow]\\\"\\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \\\"--\\\")))\\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\\\"--subsystem\\\" s]) subs)]\\n                         (System/exit\\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                         \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                         \\\"--lane\\\" \\\"cljd\\\"\\n                                         (concat sub-args flags)))))}\\n\\n  test:sub:list {:doc \\\"What test:sub would run, prerequisites and seams: bb test:sub:list <subsystem>...\\\"\\n                 :task (let [[subs flags] (split-with (fn [arg] (not (clojure.string/starts-with? arg \\\"--\\\")))\\n                                                      *command-line-args*)\\n                             sub-args (mapcat (fn [s] [\\\"--subsystem\\\" s]) subs)]\\n                         (System/exit\\n                           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\\n                                         \\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/affected.clj\\\"\\n                                         \\\"--list\\\"\\n                                         (concat sub-args flags)))))}\\n  }}\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/deps.edn (unknown)\\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \\\"1.8.741\\\"}\\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}\\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \\\"1.14.1\\\"}\\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \\\"1.0.333\\\"}\\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \\\"0.1.30\\\"}\\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \\\"1.0.7364\\\"}\\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \\\"42.7.3\\\"}\\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \\\"2.5.0\\\"}\\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \\\"2.8.0\\\"}\\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \\\"1.18.3\\\"}\\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}\\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \\\"4.13.2\\\"}\\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \\\"0.4.6\\\"}\\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \\\"1.3\\\"}\\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \\\"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\\\"\\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\\n :cljd/opts {}\\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\\n :paths [\\\"src/clj\\\" \\\"src/cljc\\\" \\\"src/cljs\\\" \\\"src/cljd\\\"\\n         \\\"build/antlr/python3/classes\\\"]\\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\\n                                        {:mvn/version \\\"0.3.0\\\"}}\\n                           :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"btree-bench\\\"]}\\n           :test {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]\\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\\n                               {:git/tag \\\"v0.5.1\\\" :git/sha \\\"dfb30dd\\\"}}\\n                  :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"cognitect.test-runner\\\"]\\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]\\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \\\"1.0.0\\\"}\\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \\\"0.58.0\\\"}}\\n                   :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"nrepl.cmdline\\\" \\\"--middleware\\\" \\\"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\\\"]}\\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\" \\\"src/dev\\\" \\\"build/antlr/python3/js\\\"]\\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"3.3.5\\\"}\\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \\\"2.0.1\\\"}\\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"0.8.280\\\"}}}\\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"3.3.5\\\"}\\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \\\"0.58.0\\\"}\\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \\\"2.0.1\\\"}\\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"0.8.280\\\"}\\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\\n                              {:mvn/version \\\"0.3.0\\\"}}\\n                 :jvm-opts [\\\"-Dconfig=config.clj\\\"]}\\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\\n                                      {:git/url \\\"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\\\"\\n                                       :sha \\\"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\\\"}\\n                                      }}\\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]\\n                  :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"cljd.build\\\"]\\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \\\"2.8.0\\\"}}\\n                    :jvm-opts [\\\"-Dconfig=config.clj\\\"]\\n                    :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"world.server\\\"]}\\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"yin.repl.main\\\"]}\\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\\n           ;; needs one.\\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\\\"src/jolt\\\" \\\"src/cljc\\\" \\\"src/clj\\\"]\\n                  :replace-deps {}}\\n           :cljs-yin-repl\\n           {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\" \\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"3.3.5\\\"}\\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \\\"2.0.1\\\"}\\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"0.8.280\\\"}}\\n            :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"yin.repl.node-runner\\\"]}\\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \\\"4.13.2\\\"}}\\n                       :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"yang-antlr-gen\\\"]}\\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \\\"2026.01.19\\\"}}\\n                   :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"clj-kondo.main\\\"]}\\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]\\n                 :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"debug-cljd\\\"]\\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"yin.repl.runner\\\"]}\\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\\n           {:main-opts  [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"cljd.build\\\"]\\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\\n                         :output-dir \\\"build/yin-repl\\\"\\n                         :output-to  \\\"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\\\"}}\\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}}\\n                       :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"dep-graph\\\"]}}}\\n\\n\\n;; clj -X:fmt\\n\\n;; clj -M:nREPL\\n\\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\\n;; clj -M:test\\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\\n\\n;; clj -X:clean\\n\\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\\n\\n\\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \\n;; mise exec -- flutter run \\n\\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \\n;; emulator -list-avds\\n\\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \\\"yin.*\\\"   # only yin namespaces\\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/mise.toml (toml)\\n[tools]\\njava = [\\\"21\\\", \\\"17\\\"]\\ncljstyle = \\\"0.17.642\\\"\\nzprint = \\\"1.3.0\\\"\\nbabashka = \\\"latest\\\"\\nclojure = \\\"1.12.4.1602\\\"\\nnode = \\\"25.6.1\\\"\\n# jolt host lane (jolt-toolchain.edn): exact pins, never \\\"latest\\\"; a change of\\n# either goes through the jolt upgrade gate\\nchezscheme = \\\"10.4.1\\\"\\ncmake = \\\"4.4.4\\\"\\nandroid-sdk = \\\"latest\\\"\\nflutter = { version = \\\"latest\\\", platforms = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n[linux-x64]\\nurl = \\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/linux/flutter_linux_{{ version }}-beta.tar.xz\\\"\\n\\n[macos-arm64]\\nurl = \\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_arm64_{{ version }}-beta.zip\\\"\\n\\n[macos-x64]\\nurl = \\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_{{ version }}-beta.zip\\\"\\n\\n[windows-x64]\\nurl = \\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/windows/flutter_windows_{{ version }}-beta.zip\\\"\\n\\\"\\\"\\\", version_json_path = \\\".releases[?channel=beta].version\\\", version_list_url = \\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/releases_macos.json\\\" }\\n\\n[env._]\\npath = [\\n  \\\"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/platform-tools\\\",\\n  \\\"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/emulator\\\",\\n]\\n\\n[env]\\n#FLUTTER_STORAGE_BASE_URL = \\\"https://storage.flutter-io.cn\\\"\\n#PUB_HOSTED_URL = \\\"https://pub.flutter-io.cn\\\"\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj (clojure)\\n;; bb smoke:jolt — the J0a minimum-baseline smoke, run UNDER jolt with the\\n;; :jolt alias (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §7.8, W8):\\n;;\\n;;   1. the :jolt alias loads yang.antlr.export and yang.antlr.packet from the\\n;;      tracked roots, with no overlay, and both answer a known value;\\n;;   2. jolt.ffi defcfn :blocking calls pass (libc usleep and strlen).\\n;;\\n;; Collect-safety is NOT asserted here: the RECORD lines show when a full\\n;; collection finishes relative to a 400 ms call in each mode, but the plain\\n;; (non-:blocking) control did not wait for its call to return on jolt\\n;; 96d7b866 (J0a round-1 report), so the observation does not yet separate\\n;; the two modes. The long-hash collect-safety gate is later J0a work.\\n;;\\n;; Prints PASS/FAIL per check and RECORD per observation; exits nonzero on any\\n;; FAIL.\\n(ns jolt-smoke\\n  (:require [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\\n\\n\\n;; Loaded here rather than in the ns form, so the libs they add are observable.\\n(def ^:private before (set (loaded-libs)))\\n(require '[yang.antlr.export :as export] '[yang.antlr.packet :as packet])\\n(def ^:private added (sort (remove before (loaded-libs))))\\n\\n(def failures (atom 0))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check\\n  [label ok? detail]\\n  (when-not ok? (swap! failures inc))\\n  (println (if ok? \\\"PASS\\\" \\\"FAIL\\\") label (pr-str detail)))\\n\\n\\n;; 1. tracked load\\n(check \\\"the closure of yang.antlr.export is exactly it and yang.antlr.packet (no transit)\\\"\\n       (= '(yang.antlr.export yang.antlr.packet) added)\\n       added)\\n\\n\\n(check \\\"yang.antlr.packet/code-points \\\\\\\"aé😀\\\\\\\" = [97 233 128512] (its :clj branch)\\\"\\n       (= [97 233 128512] (packet/code-points \\\"aé😀\\\"))\\n       (packet/code-points \\\"aé😀\\\"))\\n\\n\\n(check \\\"yang.antlr.packet/utf8-bytes \\\\\\\"aé😀\\\\\\\" = 7\\\"\\n       (= 7 (packet/utf8-bytes \\\"aé😀\\\"))\\n       (packet/utf8-bytes \\\"aé😀\\\"))\\n\\n\\n(check \\\"yang.antlr.export/byte-offsets of [97 233 128512] = [0 1 3 7]\\\"\\n       (= [0 1 3 7] (vec (export/byte-offsets [97 233 128512])))\\n       (export/byte-offsets [97 233 128512]))\\n\\n\\n;; 2. defcfn :blocking\\n(ffi/load-library)\\n(ffi/defcfn c-usleep-blocking \\\"usleep\\\" [:uint] :int :blocking)\\n(ffi/defcfn c-strlen-blocking \\\"strlen\\\" [:pointer] :size_t :blocking)\\n(ffi/defcfn c-usleep \\\"usleep\\\" [:uint] :int)\\n\\n\\n(defn- ms\\n  [t0]\\n  (long (/ (- (System/nanoTime) t0) 1e6)))\\n\\n\\n(let [t0 (System/nanoTime) r (c-usleep-blocking 200000) dt (ms t0)]\\n  (check \\\"defcfn :blocking usleep(200 ms) returns 0 after >= 200 ms\\\"\\n         (and (= 0 r) (>= dt 200)) {:result r :ms dt}))\\n\\n\\n(let [p (ffi/string->ptr \\\"a\\\\u00e9\\\\ud83d\\\\ude00\\\")\\n      r (try (c-strlen-blocking p) (finally (ffi/free p)))]\\n  (check \\\"defcfn :blocking strlen of the UTF-8 C string \\\\\\\"aé😀\\\\\\\" = 7\\\"\\n         (= 7 r) {:result r}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- collect-during\\n  \\\"On another thread run (call 400000); 50 ms in, run a full collection here.\\n   Answers the timeline in ms from the thread's start.\\\"\\n  [call]\\n  (let [t0 (System/nanoTime)\\n        log (atom [])\\n        th (Thread. (fn []\\n                      (swap! log conj [:call-start (ms t0)])\\n                      (swap! log conj [:call-result (call 400000)])\\n                      (swap! log conj [:call-end (ms t0)])))]\\n    (.start th)\\n    (Thread/sleep 50)\\n    (swap! log conj [:collect-start (ms t0)])\\n    (jolt.host/gc-full!)\\n    (swap! log conj [:collect-end (ms t0)])\\n    (.join th)\\n    (into {} @log)))\\n\\n\\n(println \\\"RECORD collect timeline, :blocking usleep(400 ms)\\\" (pr-str (collect-during c-usleep-blocking)))\\n(println \\\"RECORD collect timeline, plain usleep(400 ms)\\\" (pr-str (collect-during c-usleep)))\\n\\n(println \\\"SUMMARY\\\" (if (zero? @failures) \\\"ok\\\" (str @failures \\\" failed\\\")))\\n(System/exit (if (zero? @failures) 0 1))\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0a/src/jolt/README.md (markdown)\\n# src/jolt\\n\\nThe jolt host source root (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.1-4.2).\\nThe `:jolt` alias in `deps.edn` puts it before `src/cljc`, so a namespace here\\noverrides the portable one on jolt only.\\n\\nOnly complete, narrow host implementations live here, as `.jolt` files with the\\nsame public surface and contract tests as the portable namespace they replace.\\nSmall representation differences go in `#?(:jolt ...)` branches of the shared\\n`.cljc` source instead (`:cljd` first, then `:jolt`, then `:clj`/`:default`).\\nNever a copy of `yin.repl`, `yin.vm.engine` or `dao.jing.cbor`.\\n\\nEmpty at J0a round 1: the baseline closure (`yang.antlr.export`,\\n`yang.antlr.packet`) needs no host override.\\n\\n\"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_47b6aa5c61f14c10aa6e478b\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"collab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:18:| F1: wrong `:cmake-path` | `jolt-toolchain.edn:44` now records the observed path `~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`. This matches `bootstrap-warm-r2.log:2` and the round-1 report's Environment section. |\\ncollab/1792458769000-engineer-jolt-j0a-baseline-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md:20:| F4: missing `-Stree` log; latency quotes | `stree.log` holds the output of `jolt -Srepro -Stree -A:jolt`: nothing printed, exit 0 (the file is just `exit 0`), so the dependency tree is empty. The round-1 latencies come from the logs: `usleep(200 ms)` measured **205 ms** (`smoke-1.log`) and **200 ms** (`smoke-2.log`). I had reported 201/204, which came from runs whose output I did not save. This round's run measured 210 ms (`smoke-r2.log`). |\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"dd9fdf1a-8117-4c88-8960-7f1de1151226\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"All 5 files other than the bootstrap/toolchain are unchanged (bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, jolt_smoke.clj, README.md are identical to what I read previously — the contents match). The report r2 honestly corrects the misquotation.\\n\\nF2 bypass analysis:\\n- Exact string equality `(= origin remote)`. The cold clone uses the declared URL string as-is, so `git remote get-url origin` returns exactly that → no false mismatches on the bootstrap-created checkout (confirmed with warm-r2 exit 0).\\n- If manually cloned with `.git` suffix or trailing slash, it will mismatch → fails closed (safe, requires re-clone). No false positives from normalization: equality only holds when the stored URL matches the declaration byte-for-byte.\\n- Residual issue: redirection via `url.insteadOf` may cause the declared URL to fetch from elsewhere — however the SHA + submodule + dirty checks still constrain the contents, so it's not a substantive bypass.\\n- The negative log shows the correct reason and exit 1: \\\"has origin https://github.com/example/not-jolt, declared https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt\\\".\\n\\nF3: Recorded in the design doc §13.2:1468-1471, with a quote from the owner.\\n\\nF5: Comment inside verify! (\\\"Known gap (input to §6.4 gate hardening)...\\\").\\n\\nF4: stree.log exists (exit 0, output empty), and the r2 report corrects the latency quote with log-derived numbers (205/200/210).\\n\\nVerdict: SIGNED OFF. Under 300 words.\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:14:32 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 08:14:32 +07\\nCoding-Agent: cmd\\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\\n# Review: J0a round 2 - confirmation of fixes\\nRole: Reviewer (read-only) | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max\\n\\n## Verdict: SIGNED OFF\\n\\n| id | status | evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| F1 | CLOSED | jolt-toolchain.edn:44 now records `.../cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake`, matching bootstrap-warm-r2.log:2 and bootstrap-neg-origin.log:2. |\\n| F2 | CLOSED | jolt_bootstrap.clj `verify!` (~:107-111): `git -C dir remote get-url origin` compared by exact string equality against the declared `:origin`, failing before the SHA check. bootstrap-neg-origin.log:3-4 shows exit 1 for the right reason: `has origin https://github.com/example/not-jolt, declared https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt`. |\\n| F3 | CLOSED | docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1468-1471: \\\"Owner disposition, recorded 2026-10-20\\\" quoting the owner (\\\"confirm defaults, licensing local only, ws only. commission J0b\\\"); defaults 1-3 take effect, satisfying the §6.4/§10.1 precondition for the exact-Chez pin in worktree mise.toml:10. |\\n| F4 | CLOSED | stree.log retains the empty `-Stree -A:jolt` output (file is just `exit 0`). The r2 report:20 also corrects the round-1 latency quotes to the log-backed numbers (205/200; r2 run 210, smoke-r2.log:5) and admits 201/204 came from unsaved runs. |\\n| F5 | CLOSED | jolt_bootstrap.clj `verify!` (~:118-119) carries the comment \\\"Known gap (input to the §6.4 gate hardening): `status --porcelain` does not see changes to gitignored files inside the clone.\\\" |\\n\\n**Origin-check bypass analysis:** equality is byte-exact, so no normalization false-match. A `.git` suffix or trailing slash on a hand-made clone yields a false *mismatch*, which fails closed (re-clone needed), not a false pass; bootstrap's own cold clone stores the declared URL verbatim, so warm runs pass (bootstrap-warm-r2.log, exit 0). Residual: `url.insteadOf` rewriting could redirect fetches behind a matching origin string, but the full-SHA, submodule-map and dirty-tree checks still bind content, so it is not a practical bypass.\\n\\n**No other changes:** bb.edn, deps.edn, mise.toml, jolt_smoke.clj, src/jolt/README.md are byte-identical to round 1 on re-read; the only diffs are the two F1/F2/F5 edits plus the four new logs. Caveat: still no worktree `git status` (shell blocked); scope confirmation rests on file-level comparison and the orchestrator's re-run.\"}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792458972797,\"messageId\":\"18ef587c-b352-431e-9eeb-8bb2010459bd\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 01:31:53 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-20 08:31:53 +07\\nCoding-Agent: cmd\\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\\n# Task: independent review of J0c round 1 (ANTLR4 C++ parser feasibility ladder)\\nRole: Reviewer (adversarial, read-only)\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Assigned: 2026-10-20 08:31:53 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner routing \\\"cmd for review\\\"; author is claude-opus-5-5; resume the J0a reviewer\\n\\nReview READ-ONLY the uncommitted change in the worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c (branch jolt-j0c, base jolt-j0a 9f1f9144): modified antlr/python3/manifest.edn, bb.edn, jolt-toolchain.edn, src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj; new native/jolt-parser/CMakeLists.txt, native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp, src/dev/jolt_native.clj, src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj. Author report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792459030000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r1.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md. Spec: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md sections 6.1, 7 (7.2-7.8), 10.1 J0c row. The orchestrator re-ran the probe on macOS arm64: exit 0, six PASS lines and SUMMARY ok (tree of \\\"1 + 2\\\\n\\\" decoded in jolt; malformed \\\"1 +\\\\n\\\" returns syntax-error records, no exception).\\nScope is the FEASIBILITY LADDER only (R1 pinned runtime build, R2 real Python3 grammar generated for C++ plus helpers, R3 extern \\\"C\\\" wrapper called from jolt). Check: (a) R1: are the runtime source revision and SHA-256 really pinned and enforced (fetch only by hash, tamper case), is the build reproducible enough as claimed, are CMake/compiler flags recorded; (b) R2: the generator edit in src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj and the manifest edit touch SHARED tooling used by the existing Java/JavaScript/Dart targets: do they leave those three targets' behaviour, recorded digests and helper handling byte-for-byte unchanged? Look for any path where the existing targets' output or digests could change; check the exact-text patches for the C++ target are sound; check :license/:redistribution blocks survived the brace mistake the author reports; (c) R3: read jolt_parser.cpp adversarially: exception containment (every entry point catches everything including std::bad_alloc), buffer ownership and free path, embedded NUL and invalid UTF-8 handling, size bounds, any pointer or C++ object visible to the guest, thread/static state (ANTLR C++ shares static caches; is anything unsafe even for one worker), UB, integer overflow in length fields; (d) probe assertions: can any PASS pass while the thing is broken; (e) does the change touch anything forbidden (shared dao.stream / dao.data / dao.jing / yin.vm source, the main tree)? (f) is the report honest about what is NOT done and about unresolved helper provenance?\\nUnder 700 words, final response only (you cannot write files), header fields on top, verdict SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF, findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify.\"}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"user\",\"createdAt\":1792459918060,\"messageId\":\"35aee565-cf45-4a2d-9a62-92414437a15a\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Let's gather the files. Things to read:\\n\\n1. Author's report: