\\"    Token PositionedToken(int type, int start, int stop)\\\\n    {\\\\n        return tokenFactory.create(type, null, Pair<TokenSource?, CharStream?>(this, this.inputStream), channel, start, stop, tokenStartLine, tokenStartCharPositionInLine);\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    Token MakeCommonToken(int type, String text)\\\"]]},\\n   :generated {\\\"Python3Lexer.dart\\\"\\n               \\\"a29f3f8cceb6ec2b76185bf563d0e186bfb3d2f39cad2129c57dc31603bdb23b\\\",\\n               \\\"Python3LexerBase.dart\\\"\\n               \\\"e3b11f882d64f64d843d8ab10a133a09cb076452dc3397a6c1fc708c3c026bd5\\\",\\n               \\\"Python3Parser.dart\\\"\\n               \\\"fa00271187b2ba976be61c81acd3309b9ea8d19d458ce4a13a5ba1ed971ccf70\\\",\\n               \\\"Python3ParserBase.dart\\\"\\n               \\\"e4c4693a640e53b971d37088809c74539cc0f1dda7d9c6a3cdd9beb7ce40a87d\\\"}}},\\n ;; §4.5 license review\\n :license {\\\"Python3Lexer.g4\\\" \\\"MIT (header: Copyright (c) 2014 Bart Kiers); vendored with its notice verbatim\\\",\\n           \\\"Python3Parser.g4\\\" \\\"MIT (header: Copyright (c) 2014 Bart Kiers); vendored with its notice verbatim\\\",\\n           \\\"Java/Python3LexerBase.java\\\" \\\"no notice in file; UNRESOLVED: not vendored, fetched by pinned digest\\\",\\n           \\\"Java/Python3ParserBase.java\\\" \\\"no notice in file; UNRESOLVED: not vendored, fetched by pinned digest\\\",\\n           \\\"JavaScript/Python3LexerBase.js\\\" \\\"no notice in file; UNRESOLVED: not vendored, fetched by pinned digest\\\",\\n           \\\"JavaScript/Python3ParserBase.js\\\" \\\"no notice in file; UNRESOLVED: not vendored, fetched by pinned digest\\\",\\n           \\\"Dart/Python3LexerBase.dart\\\" \\\"no notice in file; UNRESOLVED: not vendored, fetched by pinned digest\\\",\\n           \\\"Dart/Python3ParserBase.dart\\\" \\\"no notice in file; UNRESOLVED: not vendored, fetched by pinned digest\\\",\\n           \\\"antlr4-runtime 4.13.2\\\" \\\"BSD-3-Clause\\\",\\n           \\\"antlr4 4.13.2 (npm)\\\" \\\"BSD-3-Clause\\\",\\n           \\\"antlr4 4.13.2 (pub)\\\" \\\"BSD-3-Clause\\\"},\\n ;; Generated artifacts include code derived from the two helpers, so their\\n ;; provenance must be resolved before any generated artifact is distributed.\\n :redistribution {:vendored-sources [\\\"antlr/python3/Python3Lexer.g4\\\"\\n                                     \\\"antlr/python3/Python3Parser.g4\\\"],\\n                  :generated-artifacts :none,\\n                  :blocked-until \\\"Java, JavaScript and Dart helper provenance and licence resolved\\\"}}\\n\\n\\n\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"82dfe8fa-4a97-43b2-b57a-45724553ca48\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Manifest comparison: the main tree's manifest (base) vs. the worktree's j0c manifest. The diffs are as follows:\\n- Addition of Cpp helper files and digests to :files.\\n- Addition of the :cpp target.\\n- Addition of a Cpp entry and antlr4-cpp-runtime to :license.\\n- Change to :redistribution's blocked-until: \\\"Java, JavaScript, Dart and C++ helper provenance...\\\"\\n- The Java/JS/Dart targets appear byte-for-byte identical (their digests are the same as the base: e.g., Python3Lexer.java bb61a463... identical; JS 855f47de... identical; Dart identical). Good.\\n\\nOne structural check: in the worktree's manifest, after the :dart :generated block it closes with `}}` and then continues with a cpp comment; in the base it's `}}}},`. Checking brace balance: the worktree has `:dart {... \\\"e4c4693a...\\\"}},` no wait, looking more carefully: the base's dart ends with:\\n\\n```\\n              \\\"Python3ParserBase.dart\\\"\\n              \\\"e4c4693a640e53b971d37088809c74539cc0f1dda7d9c6a3cdd9beb7ce40a87d\\\"}}},\\n```\\n(closes the dart map, the :targets map, and the comma). Worktree:\\n\\n```\\n              \\\"Python3ParserBase.dart\\\"\\n              \\\"e4c4693a640e53b971d37088809c74539cc0f1dda7d9c6a3cdd9beb7ce40a87d\\\"}}\\n```\\nThen comes the cpp comment and `:cpp {...}}},`. So the dart map closes with `}}`, and targets remains open for cpp. The cpp target ends with a `}}}},` sequence? The cpp block ends with:\\n\\n```\\n      \\\"std::unique_ptr<antlr4::CommonToken> Python3LexerBase::commonToken...\\\"]]}}},\\n```\\nThis closes the patches' string value, the patches vector, the patches map... no wait, `\\\"Cpp/Python3LexerBase.cpp\\\" [[...]]` closes with `]]`, then `}` closes the :patches map, `}` closes the :cpp map, `}` closes the :targets map, and comma. Looks correct. The author reported fixing a brace mistake and verified that all five top-level keys can be read back. The orchestrator can re-run gen to verify. Also the report says cljstyle detected it. I trust the read-back but can't execute. However the file read result shows the structure appears balanced.\\n\\nAlso, the report's defect memo says the brace mistake caused :license/:redistribution to drop out — but they exist now. F-style check (b): \\\"did the :license/:redistribution block survive the brace mistake\\\" — yes, it exists in the current file and includes the Cpp entry and updated blocked-until.\\n\\nNext, reading the remaining files: diffs of src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj (worktree vs. main tree), src/dev/jolt_native.clj, src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj, jolt-toolchain.edn (worktree j0c), diff of bb.edn. Also sections 7.2–7.7 of the spec for compliance. Also, adversarially checking jolt_parser.cpp:\\n\\nAdversarial review of the cpp:\\n1. Exception containment: jolt_parser_parse has try/catch for std::exception and (...). bad_alloc inherits from std::exception → caught. However: `message()` itself constructs a std::string and vector — if malloc fails inside hand_off, it returns -3; message() handles hand_off failure by nulling. But `std::string s(what...)` could throw bad_alloc inside the catch handler → the exception leaks outside the catch! Inside catch(...), message() constructs std::string and vector — could throw. This is a realistic (extremely rare) leak path: an exception thrown inside a catch block propagates across the extern \\\"C\\\" boundary → UB/crash. Low severity but worth pointing out. Also the construction of `Out o` inside try is fine.\\n\\n2. `hand_off` uses malloc; `jolt_parser_free` uses free — consistent. The guest copies via ffi/read-array then frees via jolt_parser_free in a finally. OK.\\n\\n3. Embedded NULs: `std::string text(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(src), len)` — length-based, preserves NULs. ANTLRInputStream from a string containing NULs: ANTLR might handle them as characters; the lexer will likely emit an error token. Policy untested (the report lists embedded NULs as unimplemented). OK — disclosed.\\n\\n4. Invalid UTF-8: ANTLRInputStream treats bytes as... actually ANTLRInputStream decodes UTF-8 into a code point array (in the C++ runtime, ANTLRInputStream(std::string) decodes as UTF-8). Invalid UTF-8 → ANTLR C++ runtime's UTF-8 decoder... might throw? Might be replaced. Unverified; report lists invalid input policy as not yet done. Disclosed.\\n\\n5. Size limits: kMaxOutput 64 MiB is checked in hand_off. But o.buf grows unbounded during walk before the check — a huge tree could OOM before reaching hand_off; bad_alloc would be caught → -2. OK.\\n\\n6. Integer overflow: `idx()` saturates to UINT32_MAX. Token start/stop: getStartIndex returns size_t; for EOF... `idx(tok->getStartIndex())`. The documentation says 0xFFFFFFFF = none. Saturation conflates \\\"none\\\" with a real index at the 4G position — not a problem at probe scale, documented. `out.u32(idx(max_type + 1))` — overflow of max_type+1 is... not a concern. u32 len cast for `o.str`: string > 4GiB is unrealistic. Text length: token text is small. OK.\\n\\nHowever, note: EOF's token type -1: `out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<int32_t>(tok->getType())))` writes -1 as 0xFFFFFFFF — the layout doc says \\\"i32 token type\\\" — fine; the probe decodes it. Wait — collision: token start/stop uses 0xFFFFFFFF = none; type 0xFFFFFFFF = EOF (-1). Consistent with the probe that names -1 as EOF.\\n\\n7. Pointer/C++ object visibility to the guest: only uint8_t* out and size. walk serializes; no pointer serialization. Tree is freed on return (unique_ptr inside ANTLR's parser? parser.file_input() returns a raw pointer owned by the parser; parser is destroyed at scope exit → tree is freed). OK.\\n\\n8. Thread/static state: per-call ANTLR runtime objects; but does the ANTLR C++ runtime have static caches? Vocabulary, rule names are static const data — read-only. BaseErrorListener is fine. For a single worker: `parser.getVocabulary()` etc. are read-only. ATN simulation state is per-parser-instance. Known: the ANTLR C++ runtime is thread-safe with respect to parser instances sharing the static ATN (the ATN is deserialized once, read-only). OK for single worker; two-worker cache isolation is listed as not yet done.\\n\\n9. UB check: `walk` uses dynamic_cast on TerminalNode and ParserRuleContext — what if the tree node is neither? ErrorNode is a subclass of TerminalNode. Root is a rule. OK. `o.buf[count_at + i]` — count_at is valid. Recursion depth of `walk` on deeply nested parse trees → stack overflow (crash, not catchable). §7.6's bounded recursion is listed as not yet done (\\\"thread/stack budget\\\"). Disclosed but worth noting: deeply nested input (e.g., thousands of nested parens) could blow the stack via recursive descent parsing itself (ANTLR's recursive-descent parser recurses) — this is inherent to ANTLR; the spec §7.6 defers it. Fine as a probe.\\n\\n10. `message()` for -2: *out holds the e.what() message buffer — does the guest read it as a JPT1 buffer? The probe must handle non-zero status differently — read as a plain string. Check the probe.\\n\\n11. `(!src && len != 0)` — if src==null and len==0, that's allowed; std::string(nullptr, 0) — is that UB? Constructing std::string from (const char*)nullptr with count 0: in C++23, std::string(nullptr) was made ill-formed; range construction [nullptr, nullptr+0)... `std::string text(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(src), len)` with src=null, len=0: per the standard, [C++23] the (const char*, size_t) constructor requires [s, s+n) to be a valid range; nullptr+0 is arguably UB pre-C++26 (P2338? actually C++23 made std::string(nullptr) delete; the (ptr, n) constructor with n=0 and ptr=null is technically UB by \\\"valid range\\\" requirement). Minor pedantic point; in practice fine. Could mention as info.\\n\\n12. hand_off's malloc(1) for the empty case — fine, avoids malloc(0) implementation-defined behavior.\\n\\n13. -4 path: bytes.size() > kMaxOutput returns -4 without freeing... nothing was allocated. *out stays null. OK.\\n\\n14. catch(...)'s message → \\\"unknown exception\\\". Good.\\n\\nNext, reading the remaining files: yang_antlr_gen.clj (both versions), jolt_native.clj, jolt_parser_probe.clj, jolt-toolchain.edn (j0c), bb.edn (j0c) tasks. Also sections 7.2–7.7 of the spec.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the generator diff, native build script, probe, toolchain, and bb.edn changes.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_c985139bfd6e4d5dbd24239a\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"paths\":[\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj\"]}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_9cec24110897474caec0f9d0\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"paths\":[\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_native.clj\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/jolt-toolchain.edn\"]}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792460014141,\"messageId\":\"6b54a19f-dfbd-410d-b55d-d289c6b94db7\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_c985139bfd6e4d5dbd24239a\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 2/2 files\\n--- File Contents ---\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj (clojure)\\n(ns yang-antlr-gen\\n  \\\"Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 parsers for every host target\\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §4.2). Reproducible from clean:\\n\\n     clj -M:antlr-gen [--grammar g] [--target java|javascript|dart|cpp]\\n                                 ; or: bb gen:antlr\\n\\n   1. Read the vendored grammars (antlr/<grammar>/*.g4, MIT, committed) and\\n      fetch the remaining pinned files at the manifest's revision (cached\\n      under build/, re-fetched only when absent); refuse any digest mismatch.\\n   2. For each manifest :targets entry (:java, :javascript, :dart), stage the\\n      grammars and that target's helpers, applying the recorded patches (the\\n      Java helpers also get their package clause prepended).\\n   3. Run the pinned ANTLR tool with the target's flags, then apply the\\n      target's recorded :output-patches to the files it wrote.\\n   4. Java only: compile with the host javac into build/antlr/<g>/classes,\\n      which deps.edn puts on the classpath.\\n   5. Digest every generated source file of the target and compare with the\\n      target's recorded :generated digests; a mismatch fails the build.\\n\\n   `clj -M:antlr-gen discover` prints the head commit of the grammar path, for\\n   deliberately moving the pin. Nothing here runs at admission time.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n    [clojure.pprint :as pprint]\\n    [clojure.string :as str])\\n  (:import\\n    (io.github.rctcwyvrn.blake3\\n      Blake3)\\n    (java.net\\n      URI)\\n    (java.net.http\\n      HttpClient\\n      HttpClient$Redirect\\n      HttpRequest\\n      HttpResponse$BodyHandlers)\\n    (javax.tools\\n      ToolProvider)))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:dynamic *grammar* \\\"python3\\\")\\n\\n\\n(defn- manifest-path\\n  []\\n  (str \\\"antlr/\\\" *grammar* \\\"/manifest.edn\\\"))\\n\\n\\n(defn- build-dir\\n  []\\n  (str \\\"build/antlr/\\\" *grammar*))\\n\\n\\n(defn- blake3\\n  [^bytes bs]\\n  (let [b (Blake3/newInstance)]\\n    (.update b bs)\\n    (.hexdigest b)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- http-get-bytes\\n  ^bytes [url]\\n  (let [client (-> (HttpClient/newBuilder)\\n                   (.followRedirects HttpClient$Redirect/NORMAL)\\n                   (.build))\\n        req (-> (HttpRequest/newBuilder (URI/create url))\\n                (.header \\\"User-Agent\\\" \\\"datomworld-yang-antlr-gen\\\")\\n                (.build))\\n        resp (.send client req (HttpResponse$BodyHandlers/ofByteArray))]\\n    (when-not (= 200 (.statusCode resp))\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Fetch failed\\\" {:url url, :status (.statusCode resp)})))\\n    (.body resp)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- read-manifest\\n  []\\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (manifest-path))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- raw-url\\n  [{:keys [repo revision path]} file]\\n  (str \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/\\\" repo \\\"/\\\" revision \\\"/\\\" path \\\"/\\\" file))\\n\\n\\n(defn- read-bytes\\n  ^bytes [f]\\n  (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath (io/file f))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- source-bytes!\\n  \\\"A pinned file's bytes: a vendored file from the repository, otherwise\\n   the build cache, fetched from the pinned revision when absent.\\\"\\n  [grammar file {:keys [vendored]} target]\\n  (cond\\n    vendored (let [bs (read-bytes vendored)]\\n               (io/copy bs target)\\n               bs)\\n    (.exists target) (read-bytes target)\\n    :else (let [bs (http-get-bytes (raw-url grammar file))]\\n            (io/copy bs target)\\n            bs)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- fetch-grammar!\\n  \\\"Each pinned file, vendored or fetched, digest-checked. A vendored file\\n   must also be ASCII (§4.5). A mismatching fetched file leaves the cache; a\\n   vendored file is never deleted.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [grammar]}]\\n  (let [src-dir (io/file (build-dir) \\\"upstream\\\")]\\n    (.mkdirs src-dir)\\n    (let [mismatches\\n          (vec (for [[file {expected :blake3, :as entry}]\\n                     (sort-by key (:files grammar))\\n                     :let [target (io/file src-dir (str/replace file \\\"/\\\" \\\"__\\\"))\\n                           bs (source-bytes! grammar file entry target)\\n                           actual (blake3 bs)\\n                           ascii? (every? #(<= 0 % 127) bs)]\\n                     :when (or (println (if (:vendored entry) \\\"vendored\\\" \\\"fetched\\\")\\n                                        file actual)\\n                               (not= expected actual)\\n                               (and (:vendored entry) (not ascii?)))]\\n                 (do (.delete target)\\n                     {:file file, :expected expected, :actual actual,\\n                      :ascii ascii?})))]\\n      (when (seq mismatches)\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"Grammar digest or ASCII check failed\\\"\\n                        {:mismatches mismatches}))))\\n    src-dir))\\n\\n\\n(defn- delete-tree!\\n  [f]\\n  (let [f (io/file f)]\\n    (when (.isDirectory f)\\n      (doseq [c (.listFiles f)] (delete-tree! c)))\\n    (.delete f)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- apply-patch\\n  \\\"One recorded exact-text replacement; the old text must occur exactly once.\\\"\\n  [file text [old new]]\\n  (let [n (count (re-seq (re-pattern (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote old))\\n                         text))]\\n    (when-not (= 1 n)\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Patch does not apply\\\" {:file file, :old old, :matches n})))\\n    (str/replace text old new)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- helper-ext\\n  [{:keys [helpers]}]\\n  (let [base (last (str/split (first helpers) #\\\"/\\\"))]\\n    (subs base (str/last-index-of base \\\".\\\"))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- target-exts\\n  \\\"The source extensions a target keeps and digests: its :exts when given\\n   (C++ keeps headers beside sources), else its helpers' extension.\\\"\\n  [target]\\n  (or (:exts target) [(helper-ext target)]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- target-dir\\n  \\\"Where a target's generated files (and copied helpers) land.\\\"\\n  ^java.io.File [{:keys [out package]}]\\n  (if package\\n    (io/file out (str/replace package \\\".\\\" \\\"/\\\"))\\n    (io/file out)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- stage-sources!\\n  \\\"Copy the grammars and the target's helpers into one generation directory,\\n   applying the recorded patches: the package clause for the Java helpers,\\n   then the target's exact-text replacements.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [grammar]} {:keys [package patches helpers]} src-dir]\\n  (let [gen-in (io/file (build-dir) \\\"grammar\\\")]\\n    (delete-tree! gen-in)\\n    (.mkdirs gen-in)\\n    (doseq [file (sort (concat (filter #(not (str/includes? % \\\"/\\\"))\\n                                       (keys (:files grammar)))\\n                               helpers))]\\n      (let [text (slurp (io/file src-dir (str/replace file \\\"/\\\" \\\"__\\\")))\\n            base (last (str/split file #\\\"/\\\"))\\n            text (if (and package (str/ends-with? base \\\".java\\\"))\\n                   (str \\\"package \\\" package \\\";\\\\n\\\" text)\\n                   text)\\n            text (reduce (partial apply-patch file)\\n                         text\\n                         (get patches file))]\\n        (spit (io/file gen-in base) text)))\\n    gen-in))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-antlr!\\n  [{:keys [grammar]} {:keys [flags helpers output-patches] :as target} gen-in]\\n  (let [out (target-dir target)\\n        exts (target-exts target)]\\n    (delete-tree! (io/file (:out target)))\\n    (.mkdirs out)\\n    (let [tool (org.antlr.v4.Tool.\\n                 (into-array String\\n                             (concat flags\\n                                     [\\\"-Xexact-output-dir\\\" \\\"-o\\\" (.getPath out)\\n                                      \\\"-lib\\\" (.getPath gen-in)]\\n                                     (map #(.getPath (io/file gen-in %))\\n                                          (:generate grammar)))))]\\n      (.processGrammarsOnCommandLine tool)\\n      (when (pos? (.getNumErrors tool))\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"ANTLR generation failed\\\"\\n                        {:errors (.getNumErrors tool)}))))\\n    (doseq [[file ps] output-patches\\n            :let [f (io/file out file)]]\\n      (spit f (reduce (partial apply-patch file) (slurp f) ps)))\\n    (doseq [h helpers\\n            :let [f (io/file gen-in (last (str/split h #\\\"/\\\")))]]\\n      (io/copy f (io/file out (.getName f))))\\n    (doseq [f (.listFiles out)\\n            :when (not-any? #(str/ends-with? (.getName f) %) exts)]\\n      (.delete f))\\n    out))\\n\\n\\n(defn- generated-digests\\n  [out exts]\\n  (into (sorted-map)\\n        (for [f (.listFiles (io/file out))\\n              :when (some #(str/ends-with? (.getName f) %) exts)]\\n          [(.getName f)\\n           (blake3 (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath f)))])))\\n\\n\\n(defn- non-ascii-files\\n  \\\"§4.5: generated textual sources stay ASCII.\\\"\\n  [out]\\n  (vec (for [f (.listFiles (io/file out))\\n             :when (some #(> (int %) 127) (slurp f))]\\n         (.getName f))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- compile-java!\\n  [pkg-dir]\\n  (let [classes (io/file (build-dir) \\\"classes\\\")\\n        compiler (ToolProvider/getSystemJavaCompiler)\\n        sources (sort (map #(.getPath %)\\n                           (filter #(str/ends-with? (.getName %) \\\".java\\\")\\n                                   (.listFiles (io/file pkg-dir)))))]\\n    (delete-tree! classes)\\n    (.mkdirs classes)\\n    (when-not compiler\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"No system Java compiler (a JDK is required)\\\" {})))\\n    (let [rc (.run compiler nil nil nil\\n                   (into-array String\\n                               (concat [\\\"-nowarn\\\" \\\"--release\\\" \\\"11\\\" \\\"-cp\\\"\\n                                        (System/getProperty \\\"java.class.path\\\")\\n                                        \\\"-d\\\" (.getPath classes)]\\n                                       sources)))]\\n      (when-not (zero? rc)\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"javac failed\\\" {:exit rc}))))\\n    classes))\\n\\n\\n(defn- generate-target!\\n  [m src-dir [tname target]]\\n  (let [gen-in (stage-sources! m target src-dir)\\n        out (run-antlr! m target gen-in)\\n        digests (generated-digests out (target-exts target))\\n        non-ascii (non-ascii-files out)]\\n    (spit (io/file out \\\"generated-digests.edn\\\")\\n          (with-out-str (pprint/pprint digests)))\\n    (when (seq non-ascii)\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Non-ASCII generated source\\\" {:target tname\\n                                                    :files non-ascii})))\\n    (when-let [expected (:generated target)]\\n      (when-not (= expected digests)\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"Generated sources differ from the recorded digests\\\"\\n                        {:target tname, :expected expected, :actual digests}))))\\n    (when (= :java tname) (compile-java! out))\\n    (println \\\"generated\\\" (count digests) (name tname) \\\"files in\\\" (.getPath out))\\n    (when-not (:generated target)\\n      (println \\\"no :generated digests recorded yet for\\\" tname \\\"; record these:\\\")\\n      (pprint/pprint digests))))\\n\\n\\n(defn generate!\\n  [only-target]\\n  (let [m (read-manifest)\\n        src-dir (fetch-grammar! m)]\\n    (doseq [t (sort-by key (:targets m))\\n            :when (or (nil? only-target) (= only-target (name (key t))))]\\n      (generate-target! m src-dir t))))\\n\\n\\n(defn discover!\\n  []\\n  (let [{:keys [grammar]} (read-manifest)\\n        url (str \\\"https://api.github.com/repos/\\\" (:repo grammar)\\n                 \\\"/commits?per_page=1&path=\\\" (:path grammar))\\n        body (String. (http-get-bytes url) \\\"UTF-8\\\")]\\n    (println (re-find #\\\"\\\\\\\"sha\\\\\\\":\\\\s*\\\\\\\"[0-9a-f]{40}\\\\\\\"\\\" body))\\n    (println (re-find #\\\"\\\\\\\"date\\\\\\\":\\\\s*\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]+\\\\\\\"\\\" body))\\n    (doseq [dir [(:path grammar) (str (:path grammar) \\\"/Java\\\")]]\\n      (let [url (str \\\"https://api.github.com/repos/\\\" (:repo grammar)\\n                     \\\"/contents/\\\" dir\\n                     (when (:revision grammar)\\n                       (str \\\"?ref=\\\" (:revision grammar))))\\n            listing (String. (http-get-bytes url) \\\"UTF-8\\\")]\\n        (println dir (mapv second (re-seq #\\\"\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\s*\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n                                          listing)))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- arg-value\\n  [args flag]\\n  (second (drop-while #(not= flag %) args)))\\n\\n\\n(defn -main\\n  [& args]\\n  (let [only-target (arg-value args \\\"--target\\\")\\n        grammars (if-let [g (arg-value args \\\"--grammar\\\")]\\n                   [g]\\n                   (sort (for [d (.listFiles (io/file \\\"antlr\\\"))\\n                               :when (.exists (io/file d \\\"manifest.edn\\\"))]\\n                           (.getName d))))]\\n    (doseq [g grammars]\\n      (binding [*grammar* g]\\n        (if (= \\\"discover\\\" (first args)) (discover!) (generate! only-target)))))\\n  (shutdown-agents))\\n\\n\\n// File: src/dev/yang_antlr_gen.clj (clojure)\\n(ns yang-antlr-gen\\n  \\\"Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 parsers for every host target\\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §4.2). Reproducible from clean:\\n\\n     clj -M:antlr-gen [--grammar g] [--target java|javascript|dart]\\n                                 ; or: bb gen:antlr\\n\\n   1. Read the vendored grammars (antlr/<grammar>/*.g4, MIT, committed) and\\n      fetch the remaining pinned files at the manifest's revision (cached\\n      under build/, re-fetched only when absent); refuse any digest mismatch.\\n   2. For each manifest :targets entry (:java, :javascript, :dart), stage the\\n      grammars and that target's helpers, applying the recorded patches (the\\n      Java helpers also get their package clause prepended).\\n   3. Run the pinned ANTLR tool with the target's flags, then apply the\\n      target's recorded :output-patches to the files it wrote.\\n   4. Java only: compile with the host javac into build/antlr/<g>/classes,\\n      which deps.edn puts on the classpath.\\n   5. Digest every generated source file of the target and compare with the\\n      target's recorded :generated digests; a mismatch fails the build.\\n\\n   `clj -M:antlr-gen discover` prints the head commit of the grammar path, for\\n   deliberately moving the pin. Nothing here runs at admission time.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n    [clojure.pprint :as pprint]\\n    [clojure.string :as str])\\n  (:import\\n    (io.github.rctcwyvrn.blake3\\n      Blake3)\\n    (java.net\\n      URI)\\n    (java.net.http\\n      HttpClient\\n      HttpClient$Redirect\\n      HttpRequest\\n      HttpResponse$BodyHandlers)\\n    (javax.tools\\n      ToolProvider)))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:dynamic *grammar* \\\"python3\\\")\\n\\n\\n(defn- manifest-path\\n  []\\n  (str \\\"antlr/\\\" *grammar* \\\"/manifest.edn\\\"))\\n\\n\\n(defn- build-dir\\n  []\\n  (str \\\"build/antlr/\\\" *grammar*))\\n\\n\\n(defn- blake3\\n  [^bytes bs]\\n  (let [b (Blake3/newInstance)]\\n    (.update b bs)\\n    (.hexdigest b)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- http-get-bytes\\n  ^bytes [url]\\n  (let [client (-> (HttpClient/newBuilder)\\n                   (.followRedirects HttpClient$Redirect/NORMAL)\\n                   (.build))\\n        req (-> (HttpRequest/newBuilder (URI/create url))\\n                (.header \\\"User-Agent\\\" \\\"datomworld-yang-antlr-gen\\\")\\n                (.build))\\n        resp (.send client req (HttpResponse$BodyHandlers/ofByteArray))]\\n    (when-not (= 200 (.statusCode resp))\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Fetch failed\\\" {:url url, :status (.statusCode resp)})))\\n    (.body resp)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- read-manifest\\n  []\\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (manifest-path))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- raw-url\\n  [{:keys [repo revision path]} file]\\n  (str \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/\\\" repo \\\"/\\\" revision \\\"/\\\" path \\\"/\\\" file))\\n\\n\\n(defn- read-bytes\\n  ^bytes [f]\\n  (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath (io/file f))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- source-bytes!\\n  \\\"A pinned file's bytes: a vendored file from the repository, otherwise\\n   the build cache, fetched from the pinned revision when absent.\\\"\\n  [grammar file {:keys [vendored]} target]\\n  (cond\\n    vendored (let [bs (read-bytes vendored)]\\n               (io/copy bs target)\\n               bs)\\n    (.exists target) (read-bytes target)\\n    :else (let [bs (http-get-bytes (raw-url grammar file))]\\n            (io/copy bs target)\\n            bs)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- fetch-grammar!\\n  \\\"Each pinned file, vendored or fetched, digest-checked. A vendored file\\n   must also be ASCII (§4.5). A mismatching fetched file leaves the cache; a\\n   vendored file is never deleted.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [grammar]}]\\n  (let [src-dir (io/file (build-dir) \\\"upstream\\\")]\\n    (.mkdirs src-dir)\\n    (let [mismatches\\n          (vec (for [[file {expected :blake3, :as entry}]\\n                     (sort-by key (:files grammar))\\n                     :let [target (io/file src-dir (str/replace file \\\"/\\\" \\\"__\\\"))\\n                           bs (source-bytes! grammar file entry target)\\n                           actual (blake3 bs)\\n                           ascii? (every? #(<= 0 % 127) bs)]\\n                     :when (or (println (if (:vendored entry) \\\"vendored\\\" \\\"fetched\\\")\\n                                        file actual)\\n                               (not= expected actual)\\n                               (and (:vendored entry) (not ascii?)))]\\n                 (do (.delete target)\\n                     {:file file, :expected expected, :actual actual,\\n                      :ascii ascii?})))]\\n      (when (seq mismatches)\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"Grammar digest or ASCII check failed\\\"\\n                        {:mismatches mismatches}))))\\n    src-dir))\\n\\n\\n(defn- delete-tree!\\n  [f]\\n  (let [f (io/file f)]\\n    (when (.isDirectory f)\\n      (doseq [c (.listFiles f)] (delete-tree! c)))\\n    (.delete f)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- apply-patch\\n  \\\"One recorded exact-text replacement; the old text must occur exactly once.\\\"\\n  [file text [old new]]\\n  (let [n (count (re-seq (re-pattern (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote old))\\n                         text))]\\n    (when-not (= 1 n)\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Patch does not apply\\\" {:file file, :old old, :matches n})))\\n    (str/replace text old new)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- helper-ext\\n  [{:keys [helpers]}]\\n  (let [base (last (str/split (first helpers) #\\\"/\\\"))]\\n    (subs base (str/last-index-of base \\\".\\\"))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- target-dir\\n  \\\"Where a target's generated files (and copied helpers) land.\\\"\\n  ^java.io.File [{:keys [out package]}]\\n  (if package\\n    (io/file out (str/replace package \\\".\\\" \\\"/\\\"))\\n    (io/file out)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- stage-sources!\\n  \\\"Copy the grammars and the target's helpers into one generation directory,\\n   applying the recorded patches: the package clause for the Java helpers,\\n   then the target's exact-text replacements.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [grammar]} {:keys [package patches helpers]} src-dir]\\n  (let [gen-in (io/file (build-dir) \\\"grammar\\\")]\\n    (delete-tree! gen-in)\\n    (.mkdirs gen-in)\\n    (doseq [file (sort (concat (filter #(not (str/includes? % \\\"/\\\"))\\n                                       (keys (:files grammar)))\\n                               helpers))]\\n      (let [text (slurp (io/file src-dir (str/replace file \\\"/\\\" \\\"__\\\")))\\n            base (last (str/split file #\\\"/\\\"))\\n            text (if (and package (str/ends-with? base \\\".java\\\"))\\n                   (str \\\"package \\\" package \\\";\\\\n\\\" text)\\n                   text)\\n            text (reduce (partial apply-patch file)\\n                         text\\n                         (get patches file))]\\n        (spit (io/file gen-in base) text)))\\n    gen-in))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-antlr!\\n  [{:keys [grammar]} {:keys [flags helpers output-patches] :as target} gen-in]\\n  (let [out (target-dir target)\\n        ext (helper-ext target)]\\n    (delete-tree! (io/file (:out target)))\\n    (.mkdirs out)\\n    (let [tool (org.antlr.v4.Tool.\\n                 (into-array String\\n                             (concat flags\\n                                     [\\\"-Xexact-output-dir\\\" \\\"-o\\\" (.getPath out)\\n                                      \\\"-lib\\\" (.getPath gen-in)]\\n                                     (map #(.getPath (io/file gen-in %))\\n                                          (:generate grammar)))))]\\n      (.processGrammarsOnCommandLine tool)\\n      (when (pos? (.getNumErrors tool))\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"ANTLR generation failed\\\"\\n                        {:errors (.getNumErrors tool)}))))\\n    (doseq [[file ps] output-patches\\n            :let [f (io/file out file)]]\\n      (spit f (reduce (partial apply-patch file) (slurp f) ps)))\\n    (doseq [h helpers\\n            :let [f (io/file gen-in (last (str/split h #\\\"/\\\")))]]\\n      (io/copy f (io/file out (.getName f))))\\n    (doseq [f (.listFiles out)\\n            :when (not (str/ends-with? (.getName f) ext))]\\n      (.delete f))\\n    out))\\n\\n\\n(defn- generated-digests\\n  [out ext]\\n  (into (sorted-map)\\n        (for [f (.listFiles (io/file out))\\n              :when (str/ends-with? (.getName f) ext)]\\n          [(.getName f)\\n           (blake3 (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath f)))])))\\n\\n\\n(defn- non-ascii-files\\n  \\\"§4.5: generated textual sources stay ASCII.\\\"\\n  [out]\\n  (vec (for [f (.listFiles (io/file out))\\n             :when (some #(> (int %) 127) (slurp f))]\\n         (.getName f))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- compile-java!\\n  [pkg-dir]\\n  (let [classes (io/file (build-dir) \\\"classes\\\")\\n        compiler (ToolProvider/getSystemJavaCompiler)\\n        sources (sort (map #(.getPath %)\\n                           (filter #(str/ends-with? (.getName %) \\\".java\\\")\\n                                   (.listFiles (io/file pkg-dir)))))]\\n    (delete-tree! classes)\\n    (.mkdirs classes)\\n    (when-not compiler\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"No system Java compiler (a JDK is required)\\\" {})))\\n    (let [rc (.run compiler nil nil nil\\n                   (into-array String\\n                               (concat [\\\"-nowarn\\\" \\\"--release\\\" \\\"11\\\" \\\"-cp\\\"\\n                                        (System/getProperty \\\"java.class.path\\\")\\n                                        \\\"-d\\\" (.getPath classes)]\\n                                       sources)))]\\n      (when-not (zero? rc)\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"javac failed\\\" {:exit rc}))))\\n    classes))\\n\\n\\n(defn- generate-target!\\n  [m src-dir [tname target]]\\n  (let [gen-in (stage-sources! m target src-dir)\\n        out (run-antlr! m target gen-in)\\n        digests (generated-digests out (helper-ext target))\\n        non-ascii (non-ascii-files out)]\\n    (spit (io/file out \\\"generated-digests.edn\\\")\\n          (with-out-str (pprint/pprint digests)))\\n    (when (seq non-ascii)\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Non-ASCII generated source\\\" {:target tname\\n                                                    :files non-ascii})))\\n    (when-let [expected (:generated target)]\\n      (when-not (= expected digests)\\n        (throw (ex-info \\\"Generated sources differ from the recorded digests\\\"\\n                        {:target tname, :expected expected, :actual digests}))))\\n    (when (= :java tname) (compile-java! out))\\n    (println \\\"generated\\\" (count digests) (name tname) \\\"files in\\\" (.getPath out))\\n    (when-not (:generated target)\\n      (println \\\"no :generated digests recorded yet for\\\" tname \\\"; record these:\\\")\\n      (pprint/pprint digests))))\\n\\n\\n(defn generate!\\n  [only-target]\\n  (let [m (read-manifest)\\n        src-dir (fetch-grammar! m)]\\n    (doseq [t (sort-by key (:targets m))\\n            :when (or (nil? only-target) (= only-target (name (key t))))]\\n      (generate-target! m src-dir t))))\\n\\n\\n(defn discover!\\n  []\\n  (let [{:keys [grammar]} (read-manifest)\\n        url (str \\\"https://api.github.com/repos/\\\" (:repo grammar)\\n                 \\\"/commits?per_page=1&path=\\\" (:path grammar))\\n        body (String. (http-get-bytes url) \\\"UTF-8\\\")]\\n    (println (re-find #\\\"\\\\\\\"sha\\\\\\\":\\\\s*\\\\\\\"[0-9a-f]{40}\\\\\\\"\\\" body))\\n    (println (re-find #\\\"\\\\\\\"date\\\\\\\":\\\\s*\\\\\\\"[^\\\\\\\"]+\\\\\\\"\\\" body))\\n    (doseq [dir [(:path grammar) (str (:path grammar) \\\"/Java\\\")]]\\n      (let [url (str \\\"https://api.github.com/repos/\\\" (:repo grammar)\\n                     \\\"/contents/\\\" dir\\n                     (when (:revision grammar)\\n                       (str \\\"?ref=\\\" (:revision grammar))))\\n            listing (String. (http-get-bytes url) \\\"UTF-8\\\")]\\n        (println dir (mapv second (re-seq #\\\"\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\s*\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]+)\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n                                          listing)))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- arg-value\\n  [args flag]\\n  (second (drop-while #(not= flag %) args)))\\n\\n\\n(defn -main\\n  [& args]\\n  (let [only-target (arg-value args \\\"--target\\\")\\n        grammars (if-let [g (arg-value args \\\"--grammar\\\")]\\n                   [g]\\n                   (sort (for [d (.listFiles (io/file \\\"antlr\\\"))\\n                               :when (.exists (io/file d \\\"manifest.edn\\\"))]\\n                           (.getName d))))]\\n    (doseq [g grammars]\\n      (binding [*grammar* g]\\n        (if (= \\\"discover\\\" (first args)) (discover!) (generate! only-target)))))\\n  (shutdown-agents))\\n\\n\"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_9cec24110897474caec0f9d0\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 3/3 files\\n--- File Contents ---\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/jolt-toolchain.edn (unknown)\\n;; The jolt host lane's toolchain declaration\\n;; (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §6.1, §6.4).\\n;;\\n;; `bb bootstrap:jolt` materializes exactly this into build/tools/jolt and\\n;; verifies it; ordinary runs never pull. Changing any pin here goes through\\n;; the upgrade gate (`qualify:jolt-upgrade`, §6.4), never silently.\\n{:jolt\\n {:origin \\\"https://github.com/jolt-lang/jolt\\\"\\n  :sha \\\"96d7b8662d7c491722445bf976b2e25e36ce5d63\\\"\\n  :committed \\\"2026-10-19T08:26:43-04:00\\\"\\n  ;; ruling 4 (§13.4): kept although untagged\\n  :tag :none\\n  :nearest-release-tag {:tag \\\"v0.8.23\\\"\\n                        :sha \\\"a0ac71c3f638fe55158bd01b4ecbb0dd3d7545e5\\\"}\\n  :describe \\\"vnightly-16-g96d7b866\\\"\\n  :dir \\\"build/tools/jolt\\\"\\n  ;; recursive submodule SHAs at :sha (git submodule status --recursive);\\n  ;; bootstrap refuses a checkout whose submodules differ\\n  :submodules {\\\"vendor/cli\\\" \\\"14f07644080070246974942415a104228d9a6b04\\\"\\n               \\\"vendor/clojure-test-suite\\\" \\\"489b6743e8421687ef96cec557830acf258d1886\\\"\\n               \\\"vendor/fs\\\" \\\"5b273b8a943a622593fbc85fca6761c5a39d6d66\\\"\\n               \\\"vendor/grenadine\\\" \\\"688e0ed6618582eccc8c8b745243ceac92835e03\\\"\\n               \\\"vendor/irregex\\\" \\\"c948a704fc732914a243c1643bfe359913d11c7b\\\"\\n               \\\"vendor/process\\\" \\\"43bdd65e189f2ccacc56662c53a21f5470ff1500\\\"\\n               \\\"vendor/sci\\\" \\\"32d62a5136ad3dc148588752f5bcc4cc30b14752\\\"}\\n  ;; proposed default 2 (§13.2): none recorded, so none applied\\n  :patches []}\\n\\n ;; Provisioned by mise from the exact pins in mise.toml. JOLT_CHEZ is always\\n ;; set explicitly (build/tools/jolt-env.sh), never left to jolt's PATH search.\\n :chez {:version \\\"10.4.1\\\"\\n        :provider :mise\\n        :mise-tool \\\"chezscheme\\\"\\n        :threaded true\\n        :binary \\\"bin/scheme\\\"}\\n :cmake {:version \\\"4.4.4\\\"\\n         :provider :mise\\n         :mise-tool \\\"cmake\\\"}\\n\\n ;; Recorded at J0a round 1 on the platforms actually run.\\n :observed\\n {:macos-arm64 {:os \\\"macOS 26.6.2 (25G83)\\\"\\n                :chez-path \\\"~/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1/bin/scheme\\\"\\n                :cmake-path \\\"~/.local/share/mise/installs/cmake/4.4.4/cmake-4.4.4-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents/bin/cmake\\\"\\n                :cc \\\"Apple clang version 21.0.0 (clang-2100.1.1.101)\\\"}\\n  ;; shiva.stigmergy.systems: not yet provisioned or run\\n  :linux-x86_64 nil}\\n\\n ;; Vendored native sources (§6.1, Q4): fetched by `bb build:jolt-native`\\n ;; only when absent from build/native/src, accepted only at the pinned\\n ;; SHA-256, built with the mise-pinned CMake into build/native/<platform>/.\\n ;; Nothing downloads during namespace loading. Not yet declared: libblake3\\n ;; and the libcrypto path/version per platform.\\n :native\\n {:antlr4-cpp-runtime\\n  {:version \\\"4.13.2\\\"\\n   :license \\\"BSD-3-Clause\\\"\\n   ;; the official C++ runtime source distribution (antlr4 doc/cpp-target.md);\\n   ;; the GitHub release carries no C++ asset\\n   :url \\\"https://www.antlr.org/download/antlr4-cpp-runtime-4.13.2-source.zip\\\"\\n   :sha256 \\\"0ed13668906e86dbc0dcddf30fdee68c10203dea4e83852b4edb810821bee3c4\\\"\\n   :upstream {:repo \\\"https://github.com/antlr/antlr4\\\"\\n              :tag \\\"4.13.2\\\"\\n              :tag-object \\\"2ac185af855ff39b4b8c41854b756767099c356f\\\"\\n              :commit \\\"cc82115a4e7f53d71d9d905caa2c2dfa4da58899\\\"\\n              :path \\\"runtime/Cpp\\\"}\\n   ;; static, position-independent: linked into the one wrapper dylib that\\n   ;; jolt loads, so no second library or rpath is resolved at load time.\\n   ;; Tests off: ANTLR_BUILD_CPP_TESTS=ON downloads googletest at configure\\n   ;; time.\\n   :cmake-flags [\\\"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\\\"\\n                 \\\"-DANTLR_BUILD_CPP_TESTS=OFF\\\"\\n                 \\\"-DANTLR_BUILD_SHARED=OFF\\\"\\n                 \\\"-DANTLR_BUILD_STATIC=ON\\\"\\n                 \\\"-DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON\\\"\\n                 \\\"-DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=17\\\"]}}}\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_native.clj (clojure)\\n(ns jolt-native\\n  \\\"bb build:jolt-native — the jolt lane's vendored native builds\\n   (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §6.1, §7.2).\\n\\n   For each source declared under :native in jolt-toolchain.edn:\\n\\n   * fetch it into build/native/src only when absent, and accept it only at\\n     the pinned SHA-256 (a mismatch deletes the download and fails);\\n   * extract it fresh and build it with the mise-pinned CMake into\\n     build/native/<platform>/;\\n   * write build/native/<platform>/build-record.edn: tool versions, flags and\\n     the SHA-256 of every output library.\\n\\n   Nothing here runs at namespace load; jolt only ever loads what this task\\n   built. Exit status is nonzero on any failure.\\\"\\n  (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\\n            [babashka.http-client :as http]\\n            [babashka.process :as p]\\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\\n            [clojure.pprint :as pprint]\\n            [clojure.string :as str])\\n  (:import (java.security MessageDigest)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- fail!\\n  [& msg]\\n  (binding [*out* *err*]\\n    (println \\\"build:jolt-native FAILED:\\\" (apply str msg)))\\n  (System/exit 1))\\n\\n\\n(defn- sh\\n  \\\"Run a command, answer trimmed stdout; fail the task on a nonzero exit.\\n   An opts map first is passed to babashka.process.\\\"\\n  [& args]\\n  (let [opts (if (map? (first args)) (first args) {})\\n        cmd (if (map? (first args)) (rest args) args)\\n        r (apply p/shell (merge {:out :string :err :string :continue true} opts) cmd)]\\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\\n      (fail! (str/join \\\" \\\" cmd) \\\" exited \\\" (:exit r) \\\"\\\\n\\\" (:out r) \\\"\\\\n\\\" (:err r)))\\n    (str/trim (or (:out r) \\\"\\\"))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run!\\n  \\\"Run a command with inherited output (long builds); fail on nonzero exit.\\\"\\n  [& cmd]\\n  (let [r (apply p/shell {:continue true} cmd)]\\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\\n      (fail! (str/join \\\" \\\" cmd) \\\" exited \\\" (:exit r)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- file-sha256\\n  [path]\\n  (let [md (MessageDigest/getInstance \\\"SHA-256\\\")]\\n    (.update md (fs/read-all-bytes path))\\n    (apply str (map #(format \\\"%02x\\\" (bit-and % 0xff)) (.digest md)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn platform\\n  \\\"build/native/<platform> name for this host.\\\"\\n  []\\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (System/getProperty \\\"os.name\\\"))\\n        arch (System/getProperty \\\"os.arch\\\")\\n        os (cond (str/includes? os \\\"mac\\\") \\\"darwin\\\"\\n                 (str/includes? os \\\"linux\\\") \\\"linux\\\"\\n                 :else (fail! \\\"unsupported OS \\\" os))\\n        arch (case arch\\n               (\\\"aarch64\\\" \\\"arm64\\\") \\\"arm64\\\"\\n               (\\\"x86_64\\\" \\\"amd64\\\") \\\"x86_64\\\"\\n               (fail! \\\"unsupported arch \\\" arch))]\\n    (str os \\\"-\\\" arch)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- mise-bin\\n  [tool version exe]\\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\\n                   \\\"mise\\\" \\\"exec\\\" (str tool \\\"@\\\" version) \\\"--\\\" \\\"which\\\" exe)]\\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\\n      (fail! \\\"mise has no \\\" tool \\\"@\\\" version \\\" installed; run `mise install \\\" tool \\\"`\\\"))\\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- fetch!\\n  \\\"The pinned source archive under build/native/src, downloaded only when\\n   absent; its SHA-256 must equal the declaration.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [url sha256] :as decl}]\\n  (let [dest (fs/path \\\"build/native/src\\\" (last (str/split url #\\\"/\\\")))]\\n    (fs/create-dirs (fs/parent dest))\\n    (when-not (fs/exists? dest)\\n      (println \\\"fetching\\\" url)\\n      (let [resp (http/get url {:as :bytes :throw false})]\\n        (when-not (= 200 (:status resp))\\n          (fail! \\\"fetch \\\" url \\\" answered \\\" (:status resp)))\\n        (fs/write-bytes dest (:body resp))))\\n    (let [actual (file-sha256 dest)]\\n      (when-not (= sha256 actual)\\n        (fs/delete dest)\\n        (fail! dest \\\" has SHA-256 \\\" actual \\\", declared \\\" sha256 \\\"; deleted\\\"))\\n      (println \\\"verified\\\" (str dest) \\\"sha256\\\" actual))\\n    (assoc decl :archive (str dest))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- build-antlr4-runtime!\\n  [{:keys [version archive cmake-flags]} cmake plat]\\n  (let [src (str (fs/path \\\"build/native/src\\\" (str \\\"antlr4-cpp-runtime-\\\" version)))\\n        out (fs/path \\\"build/native\\\" plat)\\n        bld (str (fs/path out \\\"antlr4-runtime-build\\\"))\\n        prefix (str (fs/absolutize (fs/path out \\\"antlr4-runtime\\\")))]\\n    (fs/delete-tree src)\\n    (fs/create-dirs src)\\n    (sh \\\"unzip\\\" \\\"-q\\\" archive \\\"-d\\\" src)\\n    (fs/delete-tree bld)\\n    (apply run! cmake \\\"-S\\\" src \\\"-B\\\" bld\\n           (str \\\"-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\\\" prefix)\\n           cmake-flags)\\n    (run! cmake \\\"--build\\\" bld \\\"--parallel\\\" \\\"--config\\\" \\\"Release\\\")\\n    (run! cmake \\\"--install\\\" bld \\\"--config\\\" \\\"Release\\\")\\n    (let [libs (sort (map str (fs/glob prefix \\\"lib/*antlr4*\\\")))]\\n      (when (empty? libs) (fail! \\\"no antlr4 library installed under \\\" prefix))\\n      {:prefix prefix\\n       :include (str (fs/path prefix \\\"include\\\" \\\"antlr4-runtime\\\"))\\n       :outputs (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [l] [l (file-sha256 l)])) libs)})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- build-parser!\\n  \\\"native/jolt-parser over the generated Cpp target and the pinned runtime.\\n   The generated sources come from `clj -M:antlr-gen --target cpp` (the JVM\\n   build tool); their absence fails the task rather than skipping it.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [prefix]} cmake plat]\\n  (let [gen \\\"build/antlr/python3/cpp\\\"\\n        out (fs/path \\\"build/native\\\" plat)\\n        bld (str (fs/path out \\\"jolt-parser-build\\\"))\\n        dest (str (fs/absolutize (fs/path out \\\"jolt-parser\\\")))]\\n    (when-not (seq (fs/glob gen \\\"*.cpp\\\"))\\n      (fail! \\\"no generated parser in \\\" gen \\\"; run `clj -M:antlr-gen --target cpp` first\\\"))\\n    (fs/delete-tree bld)\\n    (run! cmake \\\"-S\\\" \\\"native/jolt-parser\\\" \\\"-B\\\" bld\\n          \\\"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\\\"\\n          (str \\\"-DANTLR4_PREFIX=\\\" prefix)\\n          (str \\\"-DGENERATED_DIR=\\\" (fs/absolutize gen))\\n          (str \\\"-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\\\" dest))\\n    (run! cmake \\\"--build\\\" bld \\\"--parallel\\\" \\\"--config\\\" \\\"Release\\\")\\n    (run! cmake \\\"--install\\\" bld \\\"--config\\\" \\\"Release\\\")\\n    (let [libs (sort (map str (fs/glob dest \\\"lib/*jolt_parser*\\\")))]\\n      (when (empty? libs) (fail! \\\"no jolt_parser library installed under \\\" dest))\\n      {:prefix dest\\n       :generated (str (fs/absolutize gen))\\n       :outputs (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [l] [l (file-sha256 l)])) libs)})))\\n\\n\\n(defn -main\\n  [& _]\\n  (let [{:keys [native cmake]} (edn/read-string (slurp \\\"jolt-toolchain.edn\\\"))\\n        cmake-bin (mise-bin \\\"cmake\\\" (:version cmake) \\\"cmake\\\")\\n        plat (platform)\\n        cxx (sh \\\"c++\\\" \\\"--version\\\")\\n        runtime (fetch! (:antlr4-cpp-runtime native))\\n        built (build-antlr4-runtime! runtime cmake-bin plat)\\n        parser (build-parser! built cmake-bin plat)\\n        record {:platform plat\\n                :cmake {:path cmake-bin :version (first (str/split-lines (sh cmake-bin \\\"--version\\\")))}\\n                :cxx (first (str/split-lines cxx))\\n                :antlr4-cpp-runtime (merge (select-keys runtime [:version :url :sha256 :cmake-flags])\\n                                           built)\\n                :jolt-parser parser}\\n        record-file (str (fs/path \\\"build/native\\\" plat \\\"build-record.edn\\\"))]\\n    (spit record-file (with-out-str (pprint/pprint record)))\\n    (pprint/pprint record)\\n    (println \\\"wrote\\\" record-file)))\\n\\n\\n(apply -main *command-line-args*)\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj (clojure)\\n;; J0c round 1, rung R3: call the ANTLR4 C++ Python3 parser from jolt\\n;; (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §7.3, §7.8).\\n;;\\n;;   . build/tools/jolt-env.sh\\n;;   \\\"$JOLT_HOME\\\"/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj\\n;;\\n;; Loads build/native/<platform>/jolt-parser/lib/libjolt_parser.dylib|.so\\n;; (built by `bb build:jolt-native`), parses \\\"1 + 2\\\\n\\\" through a :blocking\\n;; defcfn, copies the private marshalling buffer into a jolt byte array, frees\\n;; it through the wrapper, and decodes it here. No native pointer leaves\\n;; `parse-bytes`. This is the feasibility probe only: no packet export, no\\n;; corpus parity, no worker caches (later J0c rounds).\\n(ns jolt-parser-probe\\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\\n            [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\\n\\n\\n(def failures (atom 0))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check\\n  [label ok? detail]\\n  (when-not ok? (swap! failures inc))\\n  (println (if ok? \\\"PASS\\\" \\\"FAIL\\\") label (pr-str detail)))\\n\\n\\n(def platform\\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (System/getProperty \\\"os.name\\\"))\\n        arch (System/getProperty \\\"os.arch\\\")]\\n    (str (if (str/includes? os \\\"mac\\\") \\\"darwin\\\" \\\"linux\\\") \\\"-\\\"\\n         (if (#{\\\"aarch64\\\" \\\"arm64\\\"} arch) \\\"arm64\\\" \\\"x86_64\\\"))))\\n\\n\\n(def library\\n  (str (System/getProperty \\\"user.dir\\\") \\\"/build/native/\\\" platform\\n       \\\"/jolt-parser/lib/libjolt_parser\\\" (if (str/starts-with? platform \\\"darwin\\\") \\\".dylib\\\" \\\".so\\\")))\\n\\n\\n(ffi/load-library library)\\n(ffi/defcfn c-parse \\\"jolt_parser_parse\\\" [:pointer :size_t :pointer :pointer] :int :blocking)\\n(ffi/defcfn c-free \\\"jolt_parser_free\\\" [:pointer] :void)\\n(ffi/defcfn c-layout-version \\\"jolt_parser_layout_version\\\" [] :int)\\n\\n\\n(defn- parse-bytes\\n  \\\"Parse the UTF-8 bytes of `source`. Answers {:status s :bytes byte-array}:\\n   the wrapper's buffer copied into jolt memory and already freed.\\\"\\n  [source]\\n  (let [src (.getBytes ^String source \\\"UTF-8\\\")\\n        n (alength src)\\n        in (ffi/alloc (max 1 n))\\n        out-cell (ffi/alloc :pointer)\\n        len-cell (ffi/alloc :size_t)]\\n    (try\\n      (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in src))\\n      (let [status (c-parse in n out-cell len-cell)\\n            p (ffi/read out-cell :pointer)\\n            len (ffi/read len-cell :size_t)]\\n        (try\\n          {:status status\\n           :bytes (if (or (ffi/null? p) (zero? len)) (byte-array 0) (ffi/read-array p len))}\\n          (finally (when-not (ffi/null? p) (c-free p)))))\\n      (finally (ffi/free in) (ffi/free out-cell) (ffi/free len-cell)))))\\n\\n\\n;; -- decoding the private layout (little-endian, see jolt_parser.cpp) ---------\\n\\n(defn- reader\\n  [^bytes bs]\\n  (let [pos (volatile! 0)\\n        u8 (fn [] (let [b (bit-and (aget bs @pos) 0xff)] (vswap! pos inc) b))\\n        u32 (fn [] (reduce (fn [acc i] (bit-or acc (bit-shift-left (u8) (* 8 i)))) 0 (range 4)))\\n        text (fn [] (let [n (u32) s (String. bs (int @pos) (int n) \\\"UTF-8\\\")] (vswap! pos + n) s))]\\n    {:u8 u8 :u32 u32 :text text :pos pos}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- decode\\n  [^bytes bs]\\n  (let [{:keys [u8 u32 text pos]} (reader bs)\\n        magic (String. bs 0 4 \\\"US-ASCII\\\")\\n        _ (vreset! pos 4)\\n        layout (u32)\\n        status (u32)\\n        rules (vec (repeatedly (u32) text))\\n        symbols (vec (repeatedly (u32) text))\\n        n (u32)\\n        nodes (vec (repeatedly n (fn []\\n                                   (if (zero? (u8))\\n                                     {:kind :rule :rule (rules (u32)) :children (u32)}\\n                                     (let [t (u32)\\n                                           t (if (> t 0x7fffffff) (- t 0x100000000) t)]\\n                                       {:kind :token\\n                                        ;; ANTLR's EOF is type -1; the packet\\n                                        ;; contract names it \\\"EOF\\\"\\n                                        :type (cond (= -1 t) \\\"EOF\\\"\\n                                                    (< -1 t (count symbols)) (symbols t)\\n                                                    :else t)\\n                                        :start (u32) :stop (u32) :text (text)})))))\\n        errors (vec (repeatedly (u32) (fn [] {:line (u32) :column (u32) :message (text)})))]\\n    {:magic magic :layout layout :status status :rule-count (count rules)\\n     :symbol-count (count symbols) :nodes nodes :errors errors\\n     :consumed @pos :length (alength bs)}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- render\\n  \\\"The preorder records as an indented tree, for the eye.\\\"\\n  [nodes]\\n  (let [out (StringBuilder.)]\\n    (loop [nodes nodes stack []]\\n      (when-let [{:keys [kind] :as node} (first nodes)]\\n        (let [depth (count stack)]\\n          (.append out (apply str (repeat depth \\\"  \\\")))\\n          (.append out (if (= :rule kind)\\n                         (:rule node)\\n                         (str (:type node) \\\" \\\" (pr-str (:text node)) \\\" [\\\" (:start node) \\\",\\\" (:stop node) \\\"]\\\")))\\n          (.append out \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n          (let [stack (if (and (= :rule kind) (pos? (:children node)))\\n                        (conj stack (:children node))\\n                        stack)\\n                stack (if (= :rule kind) stack (loop [s stack]\\n                                                 (if (empty? s) s\\n                                                     (let [s (update s (dec (count s)) dec)]\\n                                                       (if (zero? (peek s)) (recur (pop s)) s)))))\\n                ;; a rule with no children closes immediately too\\n                stack (if (and (= :rule kind) (zero? (:children node)))\\n                        (loop [s stack]\\n                          (if (empty? s) s\\n                              (let [s (update s (dec (count s)) dec)]\\n                                (if (zero? (peek s)) (recur (pop s)) s))))\\n                        stack)]\\n            (recur (rest nodes) stack)))))\\n    (str out)))\\n\\n\\n(println \\\"library\\\" library)\\n(check \\\"layout version entry answers 1\\\" (= 1 (c-layout-version)) (c-layout-version))\\n\\n\\n(let [t0 (System/nanoTime)\\n      {:keys [status bytes]} (parse-bytes \\\"1 + 2\\\\n\\\")\\n      ms (/ (- (System/nanoTime) t0) 1e6)\\n      tree (decode bytes)\\n      tokens (filterv #(= :token (:kind %)) (:nodes tree))]\\n  (println \\\"RECORD parse \\\\\\\"1 + 2\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\":\\\" {:status status :buffer-bytes (alength bytes) :ms ms})\\n  (println \\\"RECORD first 32 buffer bytes:\\\" (vec (take 32 bytes)))\\n  (print (render (:nodes tree)))\\n  (check \\\"jolt_parser_parse returned 0 and a JPT1 layout-1 buffer, consumed exactly\\\"\\n         (and (= 0 status) (= \\\"JPT1\\\" (:magic tree)) (= 1 (:layout tree))\\n              (= (:consumed tree) (:length tree)))\\n         (select-keys tree [:magic :layout :status :consumed :length]))\\n  (check \\\"no syntax errors\\\" (and (zero? (:status tree)) (empty? (:errors tree))) (:errors tree))\\n  (check \\\"root is file_input\\\" (= \\\"file_input\\\" (:rule (first (:nodes tree)))) (first (:nodes tree)))\\n  (check \\\"tokens are NUMBER 1, ADD +, NUMBER 2, NEWLINE, EOF with code-point spans\\\"\\n         (= [[\\\"NUMBER\\\" \\\"1\\\" 0 0