s.md b/collab/1793496000000-engineer-p4-checkpointB-fold.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..90da1c72\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/collab/1793496000000-engineer-p4-checkpointB-fold.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+# Checkpoint-B fold reconciliation findings\n+\n+## What failed\n+\n+The focused JVM run initially failed one assertion in\n+`p4-registry-is-inert-test`. It expected every value in `p4/generators-v1` to\n+carry `p4/banner`, but that var is the raw generator fixture definitions. The\n+folded values, including recorded oracle values and hand-pinned outputs, are in\n+`p4/all-fixtures`; unrecorded raw definitions remain `:pending`.\n+\n+## True post-fold invariants\n+\n+- `p4/awaiting-oracle` equals exactly the IDs of enabled fixtures whose folded\n+  `:oracle` is `:pending`.\n+- For each ID in `p4/recorded`, the matching folded fixture's `:out`, `:diag`,\n+  and `:uncaught` equal the recorded values. A recorded fixture has the oracle\n+  banner because it has a recorded result.\n+- Generator metadata such as `:requires` is checked on the raw\n+  `p4/generators-v1` definitions. Oracle state is checked on the generator\n+  members of `p4/all-fixtures`: the banner is expected when a record exists or\n+  an output is pinned; otherwise the fixture remains `:pending`.\n+\n+## Change made\n+\n+Updated the inert-registry description and replaced the incorrect assertion on\n+raw generator definitions with a per-fixture check against the folded\n+`p4/all-fixtures` view. The enabled-pending equality and recorded field\n+cross-check remain exact. No fixture pins or protected source files were\n+changed.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Class-model namespace: **8 tests, 587 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n+- All `programs-p4` consumer namespaces (`class-model-test`, `generators-test`,\n+  `objects-test`): **14 tests, 1,076 assertions, 6 failures, 1 error**.\n+  - Four failures are the reachable-heap stability assertion, one per VM. Each\n+    measured 151 reachable cells at 10 iterations and 5,596 at 1,000\n+    iterations, consistent with the branch's checkpoint-B heap measurement.\n+  - `objects-test` has two output mismatches (`decl-byref-param-typed-coerces`\n+    and `decl-byref-later-rejection-releases-earlier-param`) and one runtime\n+    error (`data primitive refused`, `str-concat`, wrong type). Those tests and\n+    the heap measurement are outside this task's authorized change scope.\n+- `cljstyle check test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc`: passed.\n+- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p4.cljc`:\n+  **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
